inl bless_byte_to_i32_switch () = Task ("BLESS-BYTE-TO-I32-SWITCH", "Suite, review and bless the samples/core byte_to_i32 BackendSwitch (C identical modulo variable numbering) and the comment-free samples", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,oracle", "current", "current")
inl bend_backend () = Task ("BEND-BACKEND", "Bend 2 backend named Bend, Windows-native toolchain (bun from source), as stable as Zig/Lean/Rust/C: IO codegen, unions, tuples, arrays, strings, closures, 8/16-bit ints, harness list; 2026-10-08 09:3x: 115/133 agree (was 72), 0 wrong: mutable aliased arrays as a one-slot Chan cell holding a power-of-two Bend Array (per-element-type helper set, O(log n) peek/swap, bounds abort 3), nested arrays, unions holding arrays/functions declared is Type, closures as lambdas over closure defs; harness Bend list 116 + Known bounds row; left: floats (Bend 2 has F32 only, no formatter), i64/u8, 2 raw-macro while samples, 1 macro sample; 10:1x blessed: review run and bless run identical on 2004 rows (6 FOR-D rows filtered by design), oracle now holds the 116 Bend rows; 10:2x: F32 (Bend F32 ops/compare, decimal literals with F32.neg/division for negatives, inf, nan, signed i32<->f32 helpers) -> 119/133 agree; deployed dev23; harness Bend list 120; left: f64 (no Bend F64; emulating it in F32 would change results), i64/u8, 2 mutable-layout samples, 2 raw-macro while samples, 1 raw-macro sample; 10:4x blessed C+Bend (350 rows; review and bless runs identical; the 116 earlier Bend residuals changed only by the 23-line F32 prelude); oracle holds 120 Bend rows; 13:2x coverage probe (test.ps1 -Suite examples -Native -Probe Bend, 229 Bend rows, outputs in the scratch dir): 119 agree (exactly the listed set) + 1 known, DISAGREE 0; the 108 others: 33 raw C macros/ABI, 16 negative samples rejected everywhere, 23 BackendSwitch records without a Bend key (while_* and native_cube_* assign through !!!!BackendSwitch: needs mutable locals; Rust/Python-specific samples; lib functions without Bend arms), f64 x5 (Bend 2 has only Nat/U32/F32: no faithful f64), u64 x2 (native_closure_union_rec, rust_static_closure_chain: Nat mod 2^64), the integer zoo ts_int_wrap (u8/i8 via U32 masking), layouts x4 (heap/mut records); next by unlock size: mutable locals for while/assignment, then u64 via Nat, then small ints; 17:5x u64 decision input: Bend 2 Nat is unary (type Nat: Zero | Succ, Nat.add/sub recurse per unit), so u64 via Nat is not viable; it needs a (U32, U32) two-word encoding with carry add/sub/mul and 64/32 long division, for 2 unlockable samples: parked; 2026-10-14 01:55 night ladder rung 1 (single-flight-20261014-004129, night cache, candidate from source): codegenBend gained heap and mutable layouts (a mutable record is a one-slot Chan(Array) cell of its fields through the existing array helpers; heap layouts are tuples, linear when they have more than one field so Bend's Data kind check passes), field reads by key, mutable field sets, while loops as recursive IO loops, string order via String.is_lt/le/gt/ge (code point order = C strcmp order on valid UTF-8), compound element types parenthesized in Array<(A & B)>, heap-layout default values, and an empty slice no longer checks UTF-8 boundaries (string_eq DISAGREE fixed); probe over every C sample: 343 Bend rows agree with C, 0 build-fail, DISAGREE 0 (was 119 agreeing of the listed set); harness Bend list 122 -> 344; rung 1: 3,898 rows, examples 3146 parity + 222 new (all Bend, all agree), 0 regressed/missing, native 3061 ran, oracle agree 2574, DISAGREE 0; rung 2 (gpt5parallel) and the bless pending; 2026-10-14 03:40 lane 3 night-probe Bend errors classified (C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\after-bless\\bend-arms.md) with an after-bless script bend_arms.ps1: of 31 backend-switch misses, 12 sample switches get a macro-free Bend arm (the C arm's value) and lib backend_switch/console.write_line/sm'_real append_real get Bend arms; 16 cannot be expressed today (set' reassigns a residual variable only by macro text: 12; f64 or NanIs: 3; host string parser in convert: 1); of 33 macro errors, 20 are truly C-only (spiral_abi_*, DynamicArray* helpers), 2 test macro text itself, 11 come from samples/core sm.byte_to_i32's Bend arm, which becomes !!!!Conv once codegenBend's TyConv guard accepts CharT (one-line compiler change, not applied); 2026-10-14 05:09 BLESSED: ladder rung 1 single-flight-20261014-004129 (night cache), rung 2 gpt5parallel-20261014-020116 (DISAGREE 0; 8 load timeouts on op_args_deref_if/portable_* that compile in 1.5-7 s on a quiet machine, and wgsl_record_loop's pre-existing cross-core text difference, identical in last night's rename runs), bless run single-flight-20261014-043715 in the main cache reproduces rung 1 row for row (0 of 4,094 differ); EXPECTED.tsv 3,978 -> 4,200 (+222 Bend rows, all agree with C); pre-bless copy tmp/night/EXPECTED-before-bless-night.tsv; harness Bend list 344; 2026-10-14 06:02 pack 2 (unblessed, in the source): Bend 8/16-bit ints as U32 (i8/i16 sign-extended with spiral_narrow_i8/i16, u8/u16 masked, narrowed after arithmetic, conversions, printf, defaults) and char -> i32/u32 as identity; rung 1 single-flight-20261014-051955 with -Probe Bend: 363 Bend rows agree with C (was 343), DISAGREE 0, 20 newly agreeing incl. 5 mega roots (brzozowski inventory_closed_dfa_runtime and runtime_native, lean_cic, spiral_proves, zeta runtime_native) and small_int_ops/small_int_scalar; 0 non-Bend residual changes; next: add the 20 to the Bend list, gpt5parallel rung, bless", Feature, P1, D7, 97u32, Active, "", "backend,bend", "current", "current")
