inl note_of_bend_backend_12 () = Note ("BEND-BACKEND", 12u32, "2026-10-16T13:46Z", "main-thread", "09:46 main: pack-1u installed both modes (09:16/09:21) and blessed: single-flight-20261016-092123, 6,742 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells against the pack-1s bless 073131 overridden by probes 081908 (Kotlin), 082312 (Swift), 082906 (Bend), 084211 (Python). Harness Kotlin 444, Swift 443, Bend 401, Python 422.")
inl note_of_bend_backend_13 () = Note ("BEND-BACKEND", 13u32, "2026-10-16T18:05Z", "main-thread", "14:05 main: next grain recorded, not started: i64/u64 (22 samples, 3 C-only) need a pair representation; bend2 has U32/F32/Nat only and Nat is Peano (BendTT 1n+add), so pairs of U32 like Lua's spiral_w64: add/sub with carry, 64-bit mul via 16-bit limbs, long division, signed compare, shifts, decimal show, conversions. f64 (19 samples) has no primitive at all.")
inl note_of_bend_backend_14 () = Note ("BEND-BACKEND", 14u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: Bend 2 u64 prototype (U32 & U32 pairs: add with carry, 32x32 to 64 multiply via 16-bit limbs) passes 4 BigInteger checks (job tmp/night/bend64). Syntax facts: pairs pass linearly, destructure with (+h,+l), match only on variables, shift counts are Nat.")
inl note_of_bend_backend_15 () = Note ("BEND-BACKEND", 15u32, "2026-10-17T22:16Z", "main-thread", "18:16 main-thread lab cleanup: the u64-as-U32-pairs prototype (w64_add with carry, w64_mul32 via 16-bit limbs, w64_mul, 4 self-checks exiting 0) moved from lab/bend-backend/main.bend to apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/bend/w64.bend. Its final home is the compiler's bendPrelude (emitted helpers, the way luaW64Helpers serves Lua) when the i64/u64 grain is done; that grain then deletes the lane file.")
inl compiler_upstream_onion () = Task ("COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION", "Move the compiler into the upstream fork's repo with our changes as onion layers over mrakgr's files (PR-ready), one file per backend, splitter adapted for parallel builds; 2026-10-08 first upstream-ready patch: CodegenC (user globals reach C output; (void)x in empty decref bodies, 211 -Wunused-parameter -> 0 apart from one stale output), made line-local so scripts/upstream.py exports it cleanly (4 hunks): python scripts/upstream.py export deps/The-Spiral-Language HEAD <out> --since HEAD writes The Spiral Language 2/CodegenC.fs; opening the PR on the fork is the user's call; 18:2x readable-names + C patch material now durable at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\upstream-pr\\names-and-c (CodegenC, CodegenFsharp, CodegenPython, CodegenUtils); both CodegenPython conflicts resolved by intent (fork already carries the string option source name in join_point_method); upstream.py export fix: an addition after the last line of a section goes to the end of the target file (it was spliced between codegen_env and its members); generatedMethodName uses System.Char (CodegenUtils opens only System.Text); verified by a differential build of the fork (unpatched vs patched, external includes restored from history): 0 patch-only errors, with a canary type error proving fsc reaches the codegen files past the unrelated lib/fsharp/Common.fs errors; 21:1x CodegenC now emits the backend standard includes before user globals (Seq.append globals env.globals |> Seq.distinct): user globals using bool/size_t no longer precede <stdbool.h>; dev review: only the include order changed in the 2 samples with C globals (Lean exit=-1 rows were load kills, parity alone); deployed dev32 both cores; patch material CodegenC.fs refreshed (export --since 98492a63, since the 18:34 commit moved HEAD past the names work); 19:4x two fresh candidate exports exist for the next curation pass, both exit 0 against the fork clone at polyglot/deps/The-Spiral-Language: names-and-c-194526 (export --since HEAD, so only tonight's uncommitted edits, 45634 bytes, carries the closure void-cast fix at lines 616-617 but not the committed globals fix) and names-and-c-full-194526 (export --since 98492a63, the documented PR base, 46185 bytes, carries all three: the void-cast fix, the Seq.append globals env.globals fix from C-USER-GLOBALS-DROPPED and generatedClosureName from the readable-names work); both report conflicts the fork has since moved into (14 and 20 hunks, mostly CodegenCpp plus 2-3 CodegenC hunks in the closure and string-compare areas), so the curated 10-08 names-and-c material stays canonical and opening the PR remains the user's call; 2026-10-12 split: non-defacing changes go upstream as a PR series (test-block parser skip, canonical package dirs, DeadPureLetElision, hermetic BackendSwitch, the new backends, bug fixes), each with its sample rows; edition-3 syntax stays fork-only (SPIRAL3-EDITIONS); 08:13 input from the water-oil re-shape probe: to make shared Graph/ServerUtils/WDiff upstream-shaped, hopac's supervisor must stop requiring interned path ids in shared code (42 compile errors when ServerUtils takes single-flight's text); plan: hopac keeps ids in its own layer and converts at the boundary of the shared functions; 2026-10-13 22:59 the spiral-split gear splitter (scripts/gear-dev.ps1, bench-split.ps1, build-splitter.ps1, tmp/splitter, lanes/splitter) was removed at the user's request: idle since early October (234 runs Sep 26-Oct 1, then 21), built for gpt5parallel's 159k lines; use build.ps1 -Configuration Debug -CoreSource <copy> for candidates; 2026-10-13 23:41 user decision: after hopacsota promotion (HOPACSOTA-P6); the splitter it mentions was deleted 2026-10-13", Epic, P1, D8, 10u32, Planned, "HOPACSOTA-P6,SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", "compiler,upstream", "current", "current")
