inl clean_generated_output () = Task ("CLEAN-GENERATED-OUTPUT", "Zero toolchain warnings and no comments in generated code across backends (Lean partial-def warnings suppressed by linters); 2026-10-08 13:3x measured C: the harness builds C with -w (all warnings suppressed); gcc -Wall -Wextra -fsyntax-only over the 208 committed main.c: 126 files warn (211 -Wunused-parameter, 180 -Wunused-but-set-variable); the 31 hard errors are expected (27 C-ABI samples linked with harness shims, 2 format_any lib arms deferred to the C compiler, 2 POSIX poll.h cube samples); fixes ((void)param for unused parameters, no set-but-unused temporaries) are in CodegenC = upstream section, so they go with COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION; then drop -w from the harness so warnings fail the native tier; 13:4x C -Wunused-parameter fixed: empty refcount bodies (ArrayDecrefBody, ClosureDecrefBody, heap DecrefBody) emit (void)x; (114 C outputs changed only by that line and one blank line; native unchanged); left: 180 -Wunused-but-set-variable (match results stored and never read: dead stores from peval, needs dead-store elimination), the // case comments on C switch labels (go with READABLE-GENERATED-NAMES); 18:4x fresh gcc -Wall -Wextra -fsyntax-only sweep over all 462 committed main.c: 382 clean, 31 hard errors (15 abi_external, 10 dynamic_array_growth/resize, the 2 format_any lib arms, the 2 POSIX cube samples, 2 native_managed_array_scc), 213 warnings in 49 files = 204 -Wunused-but-set-variable (was 180, new samples landed), 8 -Wunused-parameter, 1 -Wtautological-compare; two corrections to the record: the // case comments on C switch labels are gone (0 comment lines in the 462 main.c, and 0 across main.rs 402, main.pas 391, main.fsx 516, main.kt 246, main.swift 246, main.lean 135, main.wat 147, main.ts 117, main.lua 135, main.gleam 127, main.bend 120; the only comments left anywhere are the 11 main.zig build-header lines), and -Wunused-parameter is not fully fixed: the 8 remaining are closure body 