inl sample_readmes_decision () = Task ("SAMPLE-READMES", "119 older per-sample README.md files describe code in prose; delete as drift or keep (user decision); 2026-10-12 user position: no prose in repos; decide per README: fold the fact into the sample name or a test-block name, else delete (SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS); 2026-10-12 classification (keyword heuristic, list in job scratch metrics/sample-readmes.tsv): 120 READMEs = 58 descriptions (4,247 words, mostly restate the sample name) + 46 bug histories (4,435 words, \"used to\"/regressions; the commits already hold them) + 12 expectations (1,084 words: exit codes/oracle notes -> inline expectations, TEST-EXPECT-PERSIST) + 3 manual checks (2,955 words, mega_brzozowski_derivatives alone 2,677; manual steps -> automation); proposal for the user: delete the 58 descriptions now, the 46 histories once SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS gives tests descriptive names, fold the 12 expectations, automate the 3 manual checks; 2026-10-13 23:41 user decision: move every fact a README carries into its sample's names/test expectations, then delete all 119 (this is the user's OK for the tracked-file deletion); 2026-10-14 02:30 lane 3 facts-to-code mapping for all 119 READMEs (read only; C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\sample-readmes\\mapping.md, one row per sample: facts, what code/oracle/outputs already carry, the change; applied by the main thread after the bless): 20 READMEs are contradicted by the blessed oracle (9 abi_external* with Rust error and 3 Delphi 0xC0000139 crashes, dynamic_array_tuple_managed Rust exit 2, lua_while_union_pair Wasm exit 1, the closure diamond/external/transitive packages and 4 package/prototype samples all error, two Cube delay samples C build-fail on Windows); 47 describe the retired Spiral-bin C-to-Rust/Delphi lowerer (drop; their invalid.c/source.c/negative-*.c/c-shim.h inputs are dead, deletion is the main thread's call); 15 samples are 42-returning shells whose only content was the README (11 native_package_fixed_array/owned, 3 native_package_closure, rust_global_item_macro); 15 need an expectation (mostly the expected compile-error text the oracle does not store, incl. one per mega_brzozowski negative_* package, which exposes the two that fail for the wrong reason); 16 renames carry one-line intents; 10 are pure restatements; 5 files are lower-case readme.md; 2026-10-14 02:34 lane 3 note: the mapping.md summary categories overlap (one row can be contradicted, retired-lowerer and rename at once), so 20/47/15/15/16/10/2 do not sum to the 119 rows; 2026-10-14 02:57 lane 3 root causes of the 20 contradictions (C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\sample-readmes\\root-causes.md): no active silent wrong answer and no compiler bug; H1 harness: test.ps1:619 agree-fail treats any two nonzero exits as a shared failure, so a value-returning sample's wrong answer is not DISAGREE (90 C rows exit nonzero, 460 non-C rows exposed; hides lua_while_union_pair Wasm 1 vs 235); fix: only exits above 125, NTSTATUS or timeout (or a declared failure fixture) count as failures; H2 harness: bless (test.ps1:691) never drops rows for backends a sample no longer schedules: 55 stale rows (22 Rust, 22 Delphi, 11 Zig), 22 of them the abi_external* and dynamic_array_tuple_managed Rust/Delphi rows left by 20f6af8d (C-only since 2026-09-28; Delphi 0xC0000139 = old 32-bit FPC ABI, Rust exit 2 = old lowerer's refcount); H3 harness: no CFlags rule for abi_external_buffer_length_negative, so its C row is a link build-fail, not the runtime rejection (add the mutable-buffer shim rule); F1 fixtures: 9 package samples (closure diamond/external/transitive, 6 package prototype callbacks) use |core-, which resolves to deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin/core (spiral_compiler.fs:180647-180657) without the samples' +./-./=. (tmp/samples/core/operators.spi), so all rows error with Unbound variable and their negatives fail for the wrong reason; K1: cube delay C build-fail is the intended Linux-only poll.h scope (spiral_compiler.fs:177150); 2026-10-14 03:01 lane 3 addendum: all 12 oracle rows that differ from C are dispositioned (6 Known, failwith_exit shared failure, lua Wasm C2, 4 stale H2); all three latest-*.tsv show the same 8 masked rows and no c-only row that ran differently; H4 harness: test.ps1:632-635 can relabel a row that ran with a different answer as c-only (masks nothing today; restrict c-only to build-fail rows); 2026-10-14 03:14 lane 3 after-bless patch scripts (C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\after-bless, each -DryRun, exact anchors, LF; stacked on scratch copies of test.ps1, parse clean): h1_agree_fail (failure-class exits 1, 3, 134, Rust 101, Delphi FPC 200-219/227/229/231/232, negative/NTSTATUS, timeout only with timeout; C value exits 4..235 stay values; flips in today's oracle: lua_while_union_pair Wasm and the stale abi_external_struct_argument Delphi row), h2_drop_stale_rows (bless drops rows the harness no longer schedules for a sample in the run: 55 today), h3_abi_negative_flags, h4_c_only_build_fail, wasm_fixture (runner splits an exit of 126 or more into two runs, high and low nibble: lua Wasm reads 235, no residual changes; checked on scratch copies), package_samples_core (8 samples, 12 files, 28 dotted operators to upstream +,-,=), expected_errors_check (ExpectedErrors in harness.psd1 enforced as WRONG-ERROR), readme_apply (15 renames + one named literal + 6 ExpectedErrors entries, deletes 117 of 119 READMEs, keeps recursive_union_multi_case: no core so it fails on +. not on its boundary, and mega_brzozowski_derivatives: at least 6 negatives report unbound names before their intended rejection); correction: native_source_package_prototype_record_callback_missing_instance already fails for its own reason (ETY-InstanceNotFound); native_layout_stack_mutable_string_negative fails because no backend supports stack mutable layouts, not on the managed string the README names; 2026-10-14 03:21 lane 3 correct