inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_10 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 10u32, "2026-10-15T23:10Z", "lane-b", "19:1x lane-b: Kino Lua-vs-Rust probe (probe/lua_wide.spi) inconclusive: the Kino disagreement text shows both Rust and Lua values as f64 (9007199254740992.0 for 9007199254740993i64) and Lua missing the console.write line, while the same program compiled Kino-free prints exact values on Lua 5.1 and 5.4 (9007199254740993, 18446744073709551615, 9007199254740994). Follow-up: Kino-side number normalization/console.write on Lua.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_11 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 11u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: the open Kino-side doubt is resolved: lane B probe lua_wide_print passes on rust and lua with exact values; the record case (format_debug of a record holding a wide i64 printed its halves) is fixed in lib sm_real with a test (format_debug_lua_record_fields).")
