inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_1 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:33Z", "main-thread", "08:33 scoped: CodegenPython (spiral_compiler.fs ~179183-179196) emits len(s), s[i] and s[a:b]. That is two gaps, not one: code-point vs UTF-8 bytes, and Spiral StringSlice's upto is inclusive (Delphi Copy(from+1, upto-from+1), Zig/Lean upto+1) while Python s[a:b] excludes b. 2026-10-14 run: Python 22 rows, 19 agree; ts_string_slice exits 3 (Known) and ts_int_wrap exits 1 (Known, unbounded ints). Fix shape: helpers over s.encode('utf-8'): len(bytes), bytes[i] as a char, bytes[a:b+1].decode() with the bounds/continuation exit 3. Next: check whether the inclusive-upto bug alone flips ts_string_slice.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_2 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:34Z", "main-thread", "08:34 ts_string_slice is ASCII; its Known reason (code points) is wrong. The cause is the exclusive slice end: emitted v0[1:3] gives 'lp'. Source fixed (CodegenPython StringSlice -> s[a:(b) + 1]); a hand-patched main.py exits 0 like C. Lands with the next pack, which also removes the Known row. UTF-8 byte semantics remain open.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_3 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 3u32, "2026-10-14T15:38Z", "main-thread", "11:38 the corpus check (lane B's lib sweep on the pack-1b candidate) found the matching lib workaround: lib/spiral/sm'.spi slice's Python arm adds 1 to 'to' whenever a value is dynamic (to_py), compensating for the exclusive codegen. With the codegen fix the end moves twice (parsing any_string, many1_chars, between_2 fail on cuda). Codegen and lib must change together: the lib edit (drop to_py and its unused trace helper) is staged as job tmp/rotation/patches/sm-prime-slice.after.spi and applied at pack install.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_4 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 4u32, "2026-10-14T18:25Z", "main-thread", "14:24 installed with pack-1d together with lib sm'.slice (Python +1 removed): ts_string_slice Python agrees with C in single-flight-20261014-140125 and its Known row is gone; the lib parsing/sm'/runtime/guid/crypto Python tests pass (lane B corpus check). Left: UTF-8 bytes vs code points.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_5 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 5u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: Python 22 rows, 20 agree, 1 known (pack-1h oracle). Still needs the upstream PR text.")
