inl task_HOPAC_WARM_SERVER () = Task ("HOPAC-WARM-SERVER", "Make the hopac core stable as a long-lived warm server (fix 57: per-request join point state keyed per request) so harness and Kino stop paying ~10 s warm-up per process; prerequisite for Kino SOTA and for HOPAC-SPEED numbers; scoping 2026-10-08 (FRONTIER.md fix 57): warm --batch already compiles a suite 12x faster (186 s vs 2,295 s) with 1,054/1,089 rows unchanged; the ~35-100 diverging rows come from JP work items whose hard-deadline watchdog (left by a build the host abandoned) sets the process-wide terminal-failure latch inside a later build; point resets (latch, invalidation count, sequential flag, per-request watchdog ordinal) are done, tagging work items per request did not help; the remaining design is one per-BuildFile session object owning JP work items, cells, caches, deadlines and the latch, created per request and dropped after it; single-flight is already warm in the Kino daemon; 2026-10-08 12:3x DONE for the harness: host defers a failure from a process that already served a build (withholds the result, exit 4; the runner resumes that job first in a fresh process); -WarmRecycle is hopac default; same DLL -Suite all: 782 s vs 1,834 s fresh (2.35x), 2,014/2,014 rows identical (status, residual hash, verdict); 605 deferrals, 106 warm-only failures caught; remaining for Kino/fully warm (~12x): the per-BuildFile session object; 16:3x deployed hopac (CodegenC fixes + readable names) on the default warm-recycle path, -Suite all -Parallel 2: 2,024 jobs in 851 s, every oracle row in the parity class (no missing/REGRESSED), 53 parity-residual-differs = the 37 known + 14 rows of the three lib/spiral samples (variable numbering inside lib backend_switch code differs between the cores, not names); 2026-10-13 22:47 naming: the core this item calls hopac is now gpt5parallel (user decision; SPIRAL_CORE_GPT5PARALLEL, -Mode gpt5parallel, lanes/gpt5parallel); the id keeps HOPAC until eoie can rename ids (EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID); the planned rewrite is HOPACSOTA; closed 2026-10-13 23:34 as superseded by hopacsota (user decision): goal inherited by HOPACSOTA-P2 (local scheduler per compile, no per-build state leaking)", Epic, P1, D7, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,hopac,kino", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_hopac_warm_server () = Planning ("HOPAC-WARM-SERVER", Minutes 900u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Pair)
inl task_KINO_SOTA () = Task ("KINO-SOTA", "Kino to state of the art: warm compiler server, concurrent cells over a shared prefix with correct memoization (KINO-PARALLEL-CACHE), fast incremental re-run, rich outputs; acceptance test: SOCIAL-TRANSPORT-SIM scenarios pass their invariants at scale; (history audit 2026-10-12: user 06:39 asked for Kino speed and memory benchmarks: \"i'm sure erlang is not that slow if we push that kino codebase to the limit, using gleam 1.19 with subjects or something\"); 2026-10-14 04:32 lane 1 step (uncommitted): incremental reuse when one definition of a shared prefix changes; measured first (private memo dir, private daemon, scratch copy of lib/spiral, Invoke-Heavy): with today's step memo, stream.spi cold 101 s, warm 16 s (16/16 hits), convert.spi warm 20 s, but appending one unused definition to stream.spi drops every stream test (0/16 hits, 132 s) and every convert test (0/2, 87 s) because the memo key carries the whole lib package print; added a second memo level keyed by the generated code (Memo.code_result: kino identity, explicit tool paths, builder, backend, generated text, show_value, print_code, build_only, test_cell, root; only {:ok, chunk} results kept) wrapped around the target build+run in Spiral.Kino run_builder (kino.ex run_compiled), so a source edit that leaves a test's generated code unchanged skips rustc/target build and run, while compile still runs; numbers with it: stream after the unused definition 16/16 code hits, rustc+run 0 ms (cold summed 218739 ms), wall 86 s vs 155 s cold on the same loaded machine; convert after the stream edit 2/2 code hits; a real change (take_while body starts with failwith) recompiled and ran exactly sum_2,sum_3,sum_4 (the 3 tests the definition impact analysis selects) and failed exactly those, 13 code hits; two tests whose generated code coincides (zip, zip_with) share one run even cold; remaining cost after such an edit is the per-test compile (about 91 s summed for 16 tests, 4 cells in parallel); tests: memo_test adds a code_result case (hit on equal code, miss on changed code, errors never kept, off when memo is off); in a private copy run from a sibling path memo_test + kino_test + notebook_test + notebook_report_test + document_test 99/99, then landed; next step: skip the compile too for tests whose reached definitions (ZED-DEFINITION-IMPACT analysis, or compiler-provided dependencies) did not change; 2026-10-14 05:59 lane 1 step 2 (uncommitted, landed after private-copy runs): the step memo key is now reach-based: Memo.reached_program keeps only the program blocks reachable from the entry (non-definition statements, main, instances) through the identifier/operator graph, and the package part of the key is the set of package definitions reachable from that program (definition-level index of every module: blocks with names, tokens, operators; instances and non-definition statements always count; identities are module + names + occurrence, so inserting code does not shift them) instead of whole-module prints; the last step of a run is keyed on the whole source and whole package (whole_source_key), so an edit that only breaks unreached code still compiles once and fails there; numbers (memo fresh per variant, private daemons, Invoke-Heavy, machine loaded by the bless and other lanes): stream.spi unused definition appended: code memo 50 s (0/16 step hits, 16 compiles) vs reach memo 13 s and 61 s on two runs (16/16 hits, 0 compiles); take_while changed: code memo 48 s (16 compiles) vs reach 36 s and 87 s (13/16 hits, compiled exactly sum_2,sum_3,sum_4 = the 3 that fail); am'.spi unused definition: code memo 91 s (10 compiles) vs reach 6 s and 51 s (10/10 hits); slice changed: code memo 61 s vs reach 57 s and 162 s, both recompile all 10 (the global name match over-approximates: slice is a common name across lib modules), failure only in slice; broken unreached definition inserted before the last test: stream 15/16 hits, only unzip compiled and failed with the parse error; am' 9/10, only to_list compiled and failed; soundness: in every mutation the recompiled set contains every failing test (never fewer); tests: memo_test 14 (reached vs unreached definitions, instances and // inside strings, package definitions, inserted code keeps ids, whole-source key), memo + kino + notebook + notebook_report + document 104/104 from a sibling path; precision left: name matching is global across the package (am' slice/init over-approximate); next: scope unqualified names to the program, opened (-) modules and modules opened with open, and qualified m.x to module m", Epic, P1, D8, 35u32, Active, "KINO-PARALLEL-CACHE,QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER,KINO-RESULT-MEMO", "kino", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_sota () = Planning ("KINO-SOTA", Minutes 3600u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_kino_sota_1 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:03Z", "lane-b", "precision step located: memo.ex reached_package_print seeds by_name over every module of the package (roots = all identifiers in the program) and package_index drops the opened flag (for {file, _opened}); fix = key by_name per module, seed unqualified names only from opened (- / *) modules and 'open m' lines, and m.x tokens only from module m")
inl note_of_kino_sota_2 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 2u32, "2026-10-14T14:01Z", "lane-b", "scoping implemented in a private copy (memo.ex, not landed): package blocks carry their module scope; an unqualified name seeds only opened (- / *) modules plus modules named by 'open' in the code (a package block also sees its own module and its file's opens); m.x seeds only module m; memo_test 15/15 incl. a new case (unopened other.a edit keeps the key; open other, other.a and user.through via its open change it); real am'.spi mutation run waits for the gate")
inl note_of_kino_sota_3 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 3u32, "2026-10-14T18:48Z", "lane-b", "scoping landed (uncommitted, apps/kino memo.ex + memo_test.exs) after a real mutation run on a lib copy (am'.spi, 10 tests): cold 214 s; warm 10/10 hits (34 s); parsing.slice edited (a same-named def in a module am' does not open): 10/10 hits, 48 s (lane 1 measured 0/10 before); am'.slice broken: all 10 recompiled and failed with the package type error (no false hit); memo+notebook tests 54/54")
inl note_of_kino_sota_4 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 4u32, "2026-10-14T20:17Z", "lane-b", "soundness bug found and fixed (uncommitted memo.ex + memo_test): a test body without a trailing assertion is wrapped as 'inl _ = spiral_kino_test ()', which the reach memo read as a definition named _, so the body never entered the key and two such tests with the same prefix shared one result (seen: polyglot Tasks.spi 'lines' recalled 'cols' result, same 34,353 ms); 'inl _'/'inl ()' are now statements (roots); new test red before, 55/55 after")
inl note_of_kino_sota_5 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 5u32, "2026-10-15T06:36Z", "lane-b", "02:36 lane B: reach memo now takes block boundaries from the compiler (SourceBlocks, one batched --source-blocks call per run, pack-1g); re-ran the lane-1 mutation set on a private lib copy (am'.spi, 10 tests, installed 1g DLL, fresh memo): cold 148 s (214 s on 10-14 with heuristics), warm 10/10 hits 23 s (34 s), parsing.slice edited in a module am' does not open 10/10 hits 37 s (48 s), am' slice broken: 0 hits, all 10 recompiled and failed (no false hit); soundness and precision unchanged by the switch")
inl note_of_kino_sota_6 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 6u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: warm-compiler part is in (Kino runs --server-tcp compilers only; relay removed; reach memo takes boundaries from --source-blocks). Remaining big pieces: concurrent cells over a shared prefix (KINO-PARALLEL-CACHE) and QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER, now P1.")
inl note_of_kino_sota_7 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 7u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: user 21:05: Kino must be battle-tested to the fullest run: granular Spiral like lib but better, and generated target code split per unit so it compiles in parallel. History: the gpt5parallel-era F# splitter went unused (weeks of dead code) and the gear method did not make dotnet compile in parallel; eoie's crates are the working example. Rewriting the compiler through Kino under X's 280-char limit will be hard.")
inl note_of_kino_sota_8 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 8u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: memo soundness fix: editing only a test fails text used to replay a stale pass from the memo; the expectation is now part of the key (TEST-FAILS-SPECIFIC).")
inl note_of_kino_sota_9 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 9u32, "2026-10-17T11:29Z", "main-thread", "07:29 main-thread day: memo cache stability (apps/kino/lib/spiral/kino/memo.ex, tree). (1) Soundness: compiler identity was {path,size,mtime} of the 278 KB host SpiralCompiler.dll only; a core-only rebuild (11.5 MB SpiralCompilerCore.dll) would have replayed stale results. Now sha256 content of every SpiralCompiler*.dll beside the configured one, path-free. (2) Stability: source-block bounds (one dotnet --source-blocks per run, 1.3-1.7 s, a failure flipped the run to the whole-source key family) are stored in the memo dir keyed by (binaries, text). memo_test +3, 23/23, mutants killed. lib/spiral/sm'.spi memo on: cold 509 s, then 15 s and 13 s with 37/37 hits. Builds are not deterministic across cache folders, so a rebuild elsewhere re-keys (sound, costs one cold run).")
inl note_of_kino_sota_10 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 10u32, "2026-10-17T11:48Z", "main-thread", "07:48 main-thread day: per-target cost from sm' ipynb metadata (cost-report -Notebooks): gleam 27 targets 8.6 min (median 19 s), fsharp 32 / 8.1 min (15 s), cuda 27 / 5.0 min. Gleam: every cell built a fresh package (gleam_stdlib + 5 deps recompiled, 7.2 s); now up to 4 warm packages per manifest under <cache>/kino-gleam-warm with only src replaced (FileLock try-lock, all busy -> cold package): cell 9.7 s cold -> 2.9-3.1 s warm (targets_test +1). Also fixed a latent Path.wildcard-on-backslash bug in run_gleam_program. F#: cold 'dotnet fsi --exec' floor is 4.6-5.5 s of the 15 s median (rest is type-checking generated F#); a warm fsi would leak state across cells and runs against the no-interactive direction, so not built - the lever is moving F# targets to a compiled path or dropping them from default target sets.")
inl note_of_kino_sota_11 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 11u32, "2026-10-17T13:38Z", "main-thread", "09:38 main-thread day: memo cache stable end to end on the rc.2 compiler (lib/spiral/sm'.spi, 38 tests). A new compiler gives a cold run with 0 hits: 225 s, against 509 s this morning before the warm Gleam packages (Gleam median 19.2 s -> 5.6 s). The warm rerun hits 38/38 in 9 s. With SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL pointing at a byte-identical build from another cache folder it still hits 38/38 in 7 s, because the key follows compiler content now that builds are reproducible (HARNESS-RUN-ONLY-USEFUL).")
inl note_of_kino_sota_12 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 12u32, "2026-10-17T16:33Z", "main-thread", "12:33 main-thread day: the first --slowest reading of the Kino suite (167 s, 245 tests) put one test at a quarter of it: RunnerTest 'timeout kills the whole process tree' at 40.7 s, because it always waited for a fixed 40 s timeout. It now escalates the budget per attempt (8 s, then 20 s, then 40 s) and keeps its retry on a timeout that fires before the grandchild runs: 8.7 s here, passing on the first attempt, and the same 40 s ceiling under load. The next slowest are inherent (FsiSession budget kill 9.8 s is mostly dotnet fsi startup; the gleam lock and warm-package tests 8.2 and 6.5 s run real gleam builds).")
inl note_of_kino_sota_13 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 13u32, "2026-10-17T16:44Z", "main-thread", "12:44 main-thread: the Kino cache is already two-level, as the harness now is. Cell level: key = compiler binaries + reached program + bounds, so a compiler change misses. Code level: Memo.code_result, key = Kino code identity + tool options + generated code, with no compiler identity, so a compiler change that leaves a cell's generated code unchanged still replays its target run. Measured on lib/spiral/sm'.spi (38 tests): fully cold 509 s; Kino code changed (both levels miss, plus the warm Gleam packages) 225 s; compiler changed with Kino unchanged (cell misses, code hits) 83 s; nothing changed 7-9 s (38/38 cell hits); a byte-identical compiler built in another folder 7 s (38/38). Run 4's 0 code hits came from my own Kino edits that morning, not from the compiler change.")
inl note_of_kino_sota_14 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 14u32, "2026-10-17T18:24Z", "bundle-wisdom", "14:24 from the bundles (samples alpha705, brzozowski alpha54): a long-lived warm compiler session went stale and made byte-identical megas compile in 8-24 s instead of 2-4 s until idle sessions were cleaned up (--cleanup-idle --idle-ms 1); a 13-min-old session produced a false CIC 'cliff'; a stale fixed socket (/tmp/...verifier.sock) attached a new gate to an older daemon. For the warm Kino server: give each session an identity bound to the compiler/runtime fingerprint, reap stale sessions, avoid fixed global sockets, record session age in each result, and treat rc5 or timing anomalies after a long-lived session as suspect until a fresh session reproduces them (a GADT probe showed fake rc5 type errors that disappeared after shutdown).")
inl note_of_kino_sota_15 () = Note ("KINO-SOTA", 15u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 suite time is the main drag for an app with many simulation tests: one 27-test file takes 6-7 minutes memo-off, and every model change needs a full memo-off gate because the memo was unsafe across modules for a while; parallel cells and a warm server matter most.")
inl task_KINO_SPIRAL_GLEAM () = Task ("KINO-SPIRAL-GLEAM", "Experiment: Kino logic written in Spiral compiled to Gleam (BEAM), called from a thin Elixir/Livebook shim; stage two replaces Livebook runtime pieces with our own runner to drop Elixir; style reference: polyglot examples/elixir exercism multi-clause functions; user decision 2026-10-12 19:09: after the warm runner: land KINO-WARM-RUNNER in Elixir first, then port module by module to Spiral/Gleam with the existing tests as the oracle", Feature, P3, D8, 5u32, Planned, "KINO-WARM-RUNNER,KINO-WITHOUT-ELIXIR", "kino,gleam,elixir", "current", "current")
