inl fsharp_utf8_strings () = Task ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", "F# string semantics are .NET UTF-16 while Spiral strings index and measure UTF-8 bytes (C, Kotlin spiralStringIndex, Swift utf8, Wasm, Lean byte positions): 2026-10-12 once F# gained StaticStringConcat, samples/string_utf8 compiles and its .fsx exits 1 under dotnet fsi where C exits 0 (string_eq exits 0 like C); the harness never runs F# natively (test.ps1 excludes Fsharp from native jobs), so F# semantic gaps stay hidden: give F# UTF-8 byte semantics for length/index/slice (Encoding.UTF8 helpers like the Kotlin backend) and add an F# native tier through dotnet fsi or a compiled exe so F# rows are checked against the C oracle", TaskKind, P2, D4, 70u32, Active, "", "fsharp,backend,strings,harness", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fsharp_utf8_strings () = Planning ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_1 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:31Z", "main-thread", "08:31 blast radius: !!!!StringLength/StringIndex/StringSlice appear in 0 lib .spi (spiral, polyglot) and only apps/compiler/tmp/tests/rust-exports (ASCII), so byte semantics only affect samples. Codegen: both F# copies (spiral_compiler.fs ~165250/165386/165409 and ~166425/166560/166583) share one length helper for arrays and strings; plan: a stringLength arm using System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetByteCount, index via GetBytes(s).[i] as char, slice via GetString(bytes, from, upto-from+1) with the Delphi-style continuation/bounds exit 3. Next: patch both sides in the next pack, then an F# native tier (dotnet fsi) in test.ps1.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_2 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:42Z", "main-thread", "08:42 implemented in source (both core sides): StringLength -> UTF8.GetByteCount, StringIndex/StringSlice -> helpers emitted once via global' (slice exits 3 on bad bounds or a cut UTF-8 sequence, like Delphi/Lean). Array length output unchanged. Hand-built .fsx of samples/string_utf8 under dotnet fsi: exit 1 before, 0 after (= C). Lands with the next pack build; the F# native tier is still open. Char stays the unsigned byte (C sign-extends), which only matters if a char is converted to an int.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_3 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 3u32, "2026-10-14T18:24Z", "main-thread", "14:24 F# UTF-8 length/index/slice installed with pack-1d (string_utf8, string_eq and multiline_triple_string F# residuals changed and were blessed in single-flight-20261014-140125). Left: an F# native tier in test.ps1.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_4 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: F# rows still have no native tier (960 rows, 0 native). A cheap tier exists now: tonight's tmp/fsbase builds a Release exe per program from main.fsx via a one-file fsproj (11-21 s per build, runs at C-like speed). Next grain: wire that into test.ps1 as an F# native lane in chunks, like Swift.")
inl note_of_fsharp_utf8_strings_5 () = Note ("FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS", 5u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: F# rows can now be run natively (FSHARP-NATIVE-TIER prototype): of 329 F# rows with a C row, 327 agree in exit and stdout (string_utf8 included) and 2 fail to compile in fsi (FSHARP-MACRO-MUTATION); none differ.")
inl gleam_match_codegen () = Task ("GLEAM-MATCH-CODEGEN", "Gleam backend match codegen, found 2026-10-12 while writing apps/kino/spi/document.spi from_spi (both reproduce on the Kino domain build, worked around there): (1) a second match on a union already narrowed by an enclosing `| _ =>` branch emits a Gleam `case` with only the remaining arms, which Gleam rejects as inexhaustive (missing Us4InDoc/Us4InTest); emit an unreachable `_ -> panic` arm or the full case; (2) matching a single-case union returned by an inlined function (`match open_step ... with | Step (a, b, c) => ...`) emits a duplicate `_ ->` arm that references a/b/c, unbound there (Gleam: Unknown variable); a single-case union needs no default arm. Add both shapes as samples on the Gleam list; 2026-10-12 fixed by the compiler lane, committed by the user in feb8b9f7 (12:50): unbox emits no _ arm when one scrutinee covers every case and an explicit unreachable panic otherwise; samples gleam_match_narrowed / gleam_match_single_case on the Gleam list; the Gleam prelude split so spiral_math_pow is pure Gleam (gleam/float.power) and only emitted by Pow; residual: spiral_halt and 3 more Gleam prelude externals are still Erlang-only (JS-target programs that slice strings would fail); validation ladder running (compiler lane); CI confirmation 14:20: near_wallet gleam build --target javascript passes on ubuntu in run 38280264212; 17:40 compiler lane: done: a union match without fallback emits no _ arm when it covers every case of a single scrutinee, else _ -> panic \"spiral: union case ruled out by partial evaluation\" (fixes narrowed-second-match inexhaustive and duplicate _ arm with unbound vars; both reproduced pre-fix); Bend had the narrowed shape as a codegen error, now IO.die(...,3,\"\"); other backends checked fine; samples gleam_match_narrowed (exit 61) and gleam_match_single_case (exit 49) agree with C on 12 backends; ladder single-flight-20261012-115551 / hopac-122842 / restore 133540 identical on 3,793 rows, DISAGREE 0, 118 residual changes classified (94 Gleam prelude, 17 dead Dyn lets, 5 brzozowski dead unboxes, 2 omniledger F#), 24 new rows; bless deferred (two attempts hit compile timeouts under memory pressure, EXPECTED.tsv unchanged): run compiler-lane/bless-gleam2.ps1 when the gate is idle; 18:17 blessed by the compiler lane: EXPECTED.tsv changed by exactly the 118 reviewed residual-only rows + 24 new (3,874 -> 3,898 rows, nothing removed), bless run single-flight-20261012-174720 reproduces the ladder restore except 29 Calyx/Wgsl rows that are no-toolchain in the dev cache; pre-bless copy tmp/compiler-lane/EXPECTED-before-bless.tsv", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "gleam,compiler,codegen", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gleam_match_codegen () = Planning ("GLEAM-MATCH-CODEGEN", Minutes 180u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl zed_test_runnables () = Task ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", "Zed runnables for Spiral test blocks: a languages/spiral/runnables.scm query tagging `test name =` (and the file) plus a task template calling apps/kino/spi/run_notebook.ps1 --path $ZED_FILE, so a test block gets a gutter run button like Rust #[test]; needs a run_notebook --test <name> filter that runs the prefix up to that block plus its body; Livebook stays the rich-output view via --livemd-path; 2026-10-12: grammar-free first step landed (untracked): spiral/.zed/tasks.json tasks \"spiral: run test at cursor\" and \"spiral: run file tests\" call apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1 -File $ZED_FILE -Row $ZED_ROW, which resolves the test block enclosing the cursor row (header or indented body; a top-level definition row runs the whole file) and runs run_notebook.ps1 --test <name> with the ipynb in the temp dir (-DryRun prints the command; checked on math.spi rows 2/3/8/16); gutter run buttons need a real grammar: the extension borrows tree-sitter-rust (languages/spiral/config.toml grammar = \"rust\"), which cannot see `test name =` blocks (TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL); 2026-10-12 Kino lane: unblocked; run_notebook --path/--output-path/--test are stable (pass the ASCII symbol or the name); 2026-10-14 01:05 lane 1: the listed task-picker half is done (spiral/.zed/tasks.json + apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1 + run_notebook --test); the gutter half was measured against the grammar Zed actually loads (tree-sitter 0.25.10 + tree-sitter-rust 0.24.2, Zed's pinned version, in a scratch probe): Zed loads runnables.scm for extension languages (language_core queries.rs) and the test-at-row task only needs the row, so the cheapest query is ((identifier) @run @_keyword (#eq? @_keyword 'test') (#set! tag spiral-test)); over 583 .spi/.spir files (spiral lib+apps, eoie src, dice, alphabet, polyglot lib) with 375 real test blocks it matched 323 rows: 266 true, 57 false (Rust lexing of Spiral strings such as #[test] inside rust_global text, primed identifiers), 109 missed (error recovery swallows the token after a prime or a dollar-quote macro): recall 71%, precision 82%, not shippable, confirming the README; blocked on TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL; cheapest unblock found while measuring: a line-level grammar whose every token is a whole line (a prec'd test-header token beside a generic line token) makes test headers exact by construction, at the cost of the borrowed Rust highlighting (LSP semantic tokens remain); 2026-10-14 01:25 unblocked by TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL's line grammar (375/375 test headers exact on the 583-file corpus): apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral/queries/runnables.scm tags each test_header @run with its test_name as @spiral_test_name and tag spiral-test; spiral/.zed/tasks.json has a tagged task 'spiral: run test ZED_CUSTOM_spiral_test_name' running test-at-row.ps1 -Row ZED_ROW (uncommitted); gutter buttons appear once the extension switches to the grammar (needs the grammar's commit rev in extension.toml, steps in TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL) and a manual Zed check", TaskKind, P2, D3, 90u32, Active, "KINO-RUN-ONE-TEST,TEST-RUN-REPORT,TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", "zed,kino,tests", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_zed_test_runnables () = Planning ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned User)
