inl test_expect_persist () = Task ("TEST-EXPECT-PERSIST", "Expect-test mode for test blocks (user 2026-10-12): a run may write each block's observed result into the source (toggleable dev mode, ppx_expect / insta style) and clears it after a successful run; needs a result syntax under the test header that the parser skip already ignores; user decision 2026-10-12 18:53: rewrite the source, opt-in: a dev-mode flag (--accept) rewrites the _assert_eq literal in the .spi in place after a run, under a lock; without the flag a mismatch fails; git shows the diff, the user commits; 2026-10-12 19:22: dependency on SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS removed (it applies to the test blocks lib already has; the user picked it for the next session's lanes); 20:07 Kino lane (uncommitted, Spiral.Kino.Accept): --accept (.spi only, also via the warm daemon) rewrites, for each failed test whose output holds __assert_eq { actual = A; expected = E }, the single _assert_eq E literal in that test's block to A (type suffix kept), under <file>.accept.lock; rows report status accepted (counted as executed), the run exits 0 when nothing else failed; refusals per test (accept_refused: none or several matching literals, non-plain actual); without the flag a mismatch fails and the file is untouched; real run: plain exit 1, --accept exit 0 accepted 1 (_assert_eq 5i32 -> 4i32 in place), re-run 3/3 passed with memo_hits 2", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "TEST-RUN-REPORT", "tests,kino,samples", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_test_expect_persist () = Planning ("TEST-EXPECT-PERSIST", Minutes 600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
