inl note_of_configurable_oracle_5 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 5u32, "2026-10-16T18:26Z", "main-thread", "14:26 main: implemented: test.ps1 -Oracle <backend> (C default; Zig, Rust, Delphi, Wasm, Lean, Gleam, Lua, TypeScript, Python, Kotlin, Swift allowed): the oracle column compares every other native row (C included) against that backend's row; a sample without one is no-<backend>. Neutral by default (pack-1x bless 140122 reproduced its expectation with it). Coverage measured on 125241: Zig rows exist for 454 of the 493 samples with a native C row; the 39 others are C-only (22) or written for one backend (17: ebpf_*, rust_*, ts_float_nan, ts_while_loop, wgsl_parallel_lanes, python_macro_annotations); Zig arms for ts_float_nan/ts_while_loop staged in pack-1y.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_6 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 6u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: full review scored with -Oracle Zig (single-flight-20261017-043743, candidate pack): agree 5,354 (5,383 under C), known 3, no-zig 67 (C 37, Bend 12, Rust 8, Ebpf 6, Python 2, Delphi 1, Wgsl 1), DISAGREE 5, all dynamic_array_bounds_negative: Zig exits 3 on the negative index like Lean and Bend while C, Delphi, Wasm, Kotlin and Lua read out of bounds and exit 0. Zig is the stricter oracle; a switch needs Zig rows for the 67 samples and a bounds-check decision for unchecked backends.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_7 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 7u32, "2026-10-17T19:55Z", "main-thread", "15:55 main-thread, user decision 2026-10-17: Zig becomes a SECOND oracle next to C (not a replacement): reviews compare against both C and Zig rows (C fallback where no Zig row exists), roughly two native tiers per review. Evidence: today's -Oracle Zig run agreed on 5,388 rows with DISAGREE 0. Next: a -Oracle C,Zig mode in test.ps1 (both oracles scoped in Known), a Zig bless, then make it the review default; native memo keeps the second tier cheap on reruns.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_8 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 8u32, "2026-10-17T20:21Z", "main-thread", "16:21 main-thread, user decision 2026-10-17: the first Zig bless runs in the next overnight run, after the -Oracle C,Zig harness change.")
