inl spiral3_editions () = Task ("SPIRAL3-EDITIONS", "Spiral 3 as an edition of the fork, both editions in one compiler (user 2026-10-12: mrakgr has not touched the language for over a year): edition per package in package.spiproj (Rust-edition style, mixed-edition imports allowed), lexical only: the tokenizer var table (spiral_compiler.fs ~43072, words -> TokKeyword Spec*) gets an edition-3 table mapping symbol keywords to the same Spec tokens and the operator lexer consults it first, so parser/typecheck/peval/backends stay shared; start from geandra_v0_4.py FORWARD (inl :=, let :~, rec ^, union :|, match ?=, nominal :!, prototype :?, instance :+, fun \\, if ?, else |:, ...) and audit collisions per edition (=> already a match arm); keep dot record access, 2-space indent as the edition-3 formatter default (parser is column based, verify); test blocks need an edition-3 spelling; gate: spiral convert --edition 3|2 round-trips every sample and lib .spi byte for byte and both editions compile to identical residuals; 2026-10-12 first collision audit (regex lexer over 1,739 .spi in spiral lib + samples, dice/lib, eoie/src; script tmp/edition3/collisions.py): 25 of the 29 FORWARD symbols never occur as operators today (free: !+ !- &= -| :! :+ :< := :== :? :| :~ ;; ?& ?: ?= \\* \\? \\| ^ |: |? ~> ~~ ~~>); => occurs 10,932 times as the match/lambda arrow (reusing it for then/with is a parser-context question, not a lexer clash); a real clash: & is pattern conjunction (`{ level } & trace_state`, 4 uses) so `and` needs another symbol in edition 3; the ? (60) and \\ (41) hits look like $'...' macro-string escapes the regex does not model, so redo the audit with the compiler tokenizer (SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY) before deciding; 2026-10-12 18:25 main, lexical-only check (reference converter tmp/edition3/lexical.py: Spiral-style tokens = words / maximal punctuation runs / strings+comments skipped; forward = keyword words -> symbols, reverse = symbol runs -> words; exact round trip per file over apps/compiler/tmp/samples + lib/spiral, 1,269 files): with the geandra_v0_4 FORWARD table 665/1,269 round-trip; drift is dominated by => (already the match-arm/lambda arrow in 602 files, and it also stands for both then and with, so reversing needs parser context, not lexing) and & for and (pattern conjunction, plus && glue); proposed table change: then -> ?>, with -> ?|, and -> :& (all three never appear as operators in the corpus) gives 1,262/1,269; the last 7 involve fun -> \\ next to the existing !\\ inline-code operator and $'...' strings with escaped quotes that the reference converter does not skip, to be settled by the real lexer; the geandra prototype itself only round-trips 26/820 samples (whole-program parser subset: rejects nominal/union and operators like +. =. $ !!!!), so its 116 tests are frontend acceptance cases, not a converter; correction: the note above is from 18:06, not 18:25; decided by the user 2026-10-12 18:44: table changes accepted (then ?>, with ?|, and :&) and edition-3 symbols lexed in every file (edition3_symbol_token, both cores, one shared Tokenize section); a per-package edition flag only when a real conflict needs it (upstream '#' escape); 18:45 first real-compiler check (single-flight Debug, 820-sample corpus, each sample compiled as written and converted to edition 3): 590 compared before the Debug batch hit a stack overflow; 249 ok in both with byte-identical C, 340 failed identically in both (C-backend contract rejections, intended type errors), 1 difference: closure_pair_bool, where !-, glued the comma into the run '!-,'; fixed in the shared Tokenize section (a run that is a symbol followed only by commas gives the commas back); rebuild + recheck queued; 19:00 recheck with the comma fix (single-flight Debug 18:47): 590 of 820 samples compared, 250 byte-identical C in both editions (closure_pair_bool included), 340 failed identically, 0 status or text differences; the Debug batch again died with a stack overflow (0xC00000FD) around sample 591, so the last 230 need a Release build run; check script tmp/edition3/build-and-check.ps1 + check.ps1, corpus tmp/edition3/corpus; user direction 2026-10-12 19:14: edition 3 prioritizes X compatibility (a source must survive being posted to X unchanged); '#': edition 2 = upstream (literal '#' in macro strings), edition 3 never uses '#' before a letter (no hashtags), so it needs its own escape spelling; this is the first real reason for the per-package edition flag; 20:03 edition-3 lexing verified harmless for edition 2 by single-flight-20261012-193841 (-Suite all -Native, Release built 19:36 from the source with the unified Tokenize section, edition-3 symbols + comma fix, WGSL nullary unions and the FOR-D offside fix): 3,799 jobs, baseline parity 3,793 / new 6 / missing+regressed 0 / residual-differs 0, native 2,775 ran, 11 build-fail, oracle agree 2,307, DISAGREE 0, 23 min: every existing row is byte-identical to the blessed oracle; 22:46 edition-3 lexing Release check (single-flight 22:26 DLL): 743 of 820 corpus samples: 363 identical C, 379 fail identically in both editions, 0 C text differences; the batch died at runaway_inline_match_recursion (e2 timeout, exit 3); the remaining 155 jobs (tmp/edition3/corpus/jobs-remaining.tsv) rerun after the InlineDepth guard; 00:07 edition-3 lexing check COMPLETE on Release: all 820 corpus samples: 438 identical C, 381 fail identically in both editions, 0 C text differences; the only status difference is runaway_inline_match_recursion (e2 timed out on the old 22:26 DLL, e3 stopped with EJP0011 on the 00:04 DLL with the InlineDepth guard), a DLL difference, not lexing; 2026-10-13 12:35 main: concrete first use: upstream programs (Spiral-s-ML-Library head) need prefix * = RawLayoutIndex (var or parenthesised term), while the fork's lib needs * = user ~* over the application chain; the parser plumbing (RawLayoutIndex through Infer/Prepass, ETY-ExpectedLayout) is in both cores, only the surface case needs the edition switch; Kino already reads edition: 3 from package.spiproj for X-compat; 2026-10-13 18:05 main: first switch landed and blessed (pack 3): DefaultEnv.edition (SpiralEdition = UpstreamEdition2 | ForkEdition3), --edition 2|3 on the host / SPIRAL_EDITION, default 3; edition 2 parses prefix * as upstream's layout index; lib/spiral unaffected (lib smoke green both cores); next candidates for the switch: '#' inside macro strings, edition3_symbol_token keywords", Epic, P1, D7, 35u32, Active, "SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY", "compiler,edition,syntax", "current", "current")
