inl hopac_coordination_kernel () = Task ("HOPAC-COORDINATION-KERNEL", "A reference state machine for the hopac model (choices with losing alternatives, shared result cells, cancellation scopes, owned evaluation contexts; cancellation requested != task finished != state reclaimable), with the fork's documented failures as the regression corpus (shared fresh-ID counters, duplicate parent replay, incomplete placeholders, cross-build contamination fix 57); then Rust (crossbeam, arenas matched to protocol lifetimes) and Gleam (subjects) implementations compared by event histories, clean vs incremental, sequential vs parallel; related: HOPAC-WARM-SERVER (fix 57 is one of the corpus failures) and KINO-SPIRAL-GLEAM (the Gleam side shares the subject-based runtime); 2026-10-13 22:47 naming: the core this item calls hopac is now gpt5parallel (user decision; SPIRAL_CORE_GPT5PARALLEL, -Mode gpt5parallel, lanes/gpt5parallel); the id keeps HOPAC until eoie can rename ids (EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID); the planned rewrite is HOPACSOTA; closed 2026-10-13 23:34 as superseded by hopacsota (user decision): goal inherited by HOPACSOTA-P2 (D3/D4 fill-once cells, wait-for server)", Feature, P2, D7, 100u32, Done, "", "hopac,concurrency,rust,gleam", "current", "current")
