inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: status was stale (Planned 0%). Verdicts so far: walk steps pinned; step timing and road speed hold (PC-1, PC-2); monster wake holds; melee hit distribution holds (33.6 vs 34.97); swing delay after a step holds (PC-3); potion use still off for retreat (POTION-FIDELITY).")
inl tibia_baselines () = Task ("TIBIA-BASELINES", "Arena baselines on a frozen scenario pack: headless protocol client (Spiral/Rust), nExBot (github.com/mCodex/nExBot, pushed 2026-09-01, no license file detected: confirm), vBot (OTClient Redemption 4.1 ships mods/game_bot with default_configs/vBot_4.8 and cavebot_1.3, so it runs on Canary's protocol 1511; also in OTCv8/otclientv8, which stops at 11.x), a scripted cavebot, a random-policy control; parity rules (15x11 view, one action-rate cap, same character/supplies/seeds); real-time evaluation budget ~150 h of play per pass at 2-3 client+server pairs; 2026-10-13 07:46 first baseline live: vBot_4.8 (OTClient Redemption's mods/game_bot) runs headless-configured through tibia-local/run-policy-scenario.ps1 -Bot vBot (fresh copy of the shipped config, TargetBot config vbot-arena.json: troll, chase, priority 1; storage enables it; probe-vbot-body.lua only enables the bot through g_settings and observes); 3 trolls, balanced, axe 30: vBot +90 experience (3 kills) in ~105 s, lowest health 181; the Spiral policy (CurrentFirst) +90 (3 kills) in ~103 s, lowest 178: a tie on this small scenario; next: the parity layer (action-rate cap, 15x11 view) and harder scenarios (cyclops, mixed packs) with seeds; 2026-10-13 08:44 parity layer live (tibia-local/parity.lua, prepended to every probe unless -NoParity): one shared gate admits at most one action per 250 ms across g_game attack/follow/walk/turn/talk/use*/move/cancel* and LocalPlayer.autoWalk, and g_map.getSpectators returns only creatures within the 15x11 client screen; 3 trolls under parity: vBot +90 experience in ~80 s (17 actions allowed, 7 dropped), Spiral policy +90 in ~90 s (16 allowed, 5 dropped); next: repeated seeds per competitor and harder scenarios (vBot needs HealBot configured for anything dangerous); 2026-10-13 09:26 first repeated arena table (tibia-local/run-arena.ps1, 5 alternating runs each, 3 trolls, parity on, policy compiled from a snapshot; arena-results.tsv): full clears Spiral 4/5 (mean 92.1 s over full clears, actions 15.2), vBot 5/5 (mean 108.0 s, sd 21.7, actions 22.8); Spiral's missed clear came from its own stop rule (no visible target) when a fleeing troll left the 15x11 parity view; the stop rule is now full experience for both; no significant difference at n=5; next: more runs, the harder cyclops scenario (vBot needs HealBot); 2026-10-13 10:06 cyclops arena harness: run-policy-scenario.ps1 gains -Level (experience, max health 185+15(L-8), mana derived), -HealBelow/-StrikeAbove (TIBIA_ARENA_HEAL_BELOW/STRIKE_ABOVE read by both probe bodies, troll defaults unchanged), potion 266 restocked to 100 in the reset, vBot TargetBot regex from -Monster and a seeded HealBot.json (potion 266 below the same hp threshold, profiles 0 and 1); run-arena.ps1 passes them through, sets the full-experience stop rule, and keeps every run's full output in tibia-local/arena-logs; smoke round (level 30, axe 60, 3 cyclops, heal below 150): BOTH competitors died within 10 s of the summon (vBot log: dead before t=10s, 7 actions), while the simulator's same knight survives most 5-minute hunts; potion (125-175) and cyclops melee (0-105 per 2 s) match Canary's scripts, so the gap is elsewhere (heals not landing live, or extra damage); diagnosis run was reaped for low memory at 10:05, retry after the compiler chain frees memory; 2026-10-13 10:17 cyclops smoke deaths explained: (1) no potions: deaths in earlier runs dropped the backpack's contents and the reset only updated an existing row, so the 'Sorry, not possible' heal had nothing to drink; the reset now deletes and re-inserts 100 potions in the backpack (verified live: 'Using one of 100 health potions', heals 141-170); (2) the probe marked a heal done even when the parity gate dropped it; it now retries next tick; (3) a cyclops kill gives 225 experience on this server (rate stage), so three cyclops need -FullExperience 675; 2026-10-13 12:19 cyclops clear arena v1 (BENCHMARK pack v1 'cyclops clear', forge off, heal below 70 for all, tibia-local/arena-results-cyclops.tsv since 11:35, arena-summary.ps1): kiting network 4/5 cleared, 85.5 +- 8.2 s, 13.6 +- 4.4 potions, 2425 +- 634 damage; rules 4/5, 92.7 +- 15.2 s, 14.2 +- 1.9, 2506 +- 232; vBot 3/4, 90.0 +- 17.3 s, 12.0 +- 6.9; every competitor died once; no significant separation at n=4-5 (the first-run kiting gain was noise); heal 70 is unsafe live, which the simulator missed (fixed since: Canary block charges, diagonal x3 and chase x2 steps, the 250 ms action gap as a typed readiness witness, live spawn layout); harness fixes during v1: vBot HealBot Visible=false, vBot probe logs damage, -Competitors parsing; v2 next: probe retreats only onto walkable tiles (live kiting walked into walls), threshold re-tuned on the corrected simulator; 2026-10-13 13:39 cyclops clear arena v2 (heal below 100 for all, probe v2 with walkable retreats, arena-results-cyclops-v2.tsv): vBot 5/5 cleared, 0 deaths, 88.0 +- 11.0 s, 15.8 +- 4.3 potions; rules 4/5, 1 death (that run also had the parity gate reporting admitted potions as dropped, fixed 13:12), 86.6 +- 4.9 s, 14.2 +- 6.5; kiting 2/5, 3 deaths (the simulator also ranks it worst; the arena spot is walled in, 38 of 39 retreat decisions found no walkable tile); harness asymmetry found: vBot's HealBot macro runs every 100 ms while our probe decided every 250 ms, both behind the same 250 ms action gate, so vBot reacted faster to bursts; the probe now ticks every 100 ms like vBot (the gate still caps actions), and clear time is measured in ms by both probes; v3 next: rules vs vBot only; 2026-10-13 14:16 cyclops clear arena v3 (first with matched decision rates: our probe ticks every 100 ms like vBot's HealBot macro, same 250 ms action gate, heal below 100 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v3.tsv): Spiral rules 4/5 cleared, 80.1 +- 7.0 s, 13.4 +- 6.3 potions, 2369 +- 871 damage, 1 death; vBot 4/5, 90.0 +- 11.5 s, 13.8 +- 6.3, 2461 +- 882, 1 death; clear-time difference not significant (Welch t = -1.47, n = 4 each); next: 10+ runs per competitor before claiming a gap, and the simulator's learned policies once they dominate by more than noise; 2026-10-13 14:46 ARENA DATA INVALIDATED after 12:02: deaths dropped the knight's equipment (no blessings) and the reset restored only potions, so from the first death on the knight fought with less gear (clean runs: 33.6 mean per landed hit, max 86; afterwards 38-45, max up to 101; by 14:27 helmet, armor, legs, shield and backpack were all gone and every run died with 0 potions); v1 rows after 12:02, all of v2 and v3 are void (files renamed *-gear-lost-invalid); the reset now deletes the knight's items and inserts the canonical set (brass helmet, backpack, brass armor, dwarven shield, steel axe, brass legs, leather boots, store inbox, 100 potions); also void: the 'live mean 37.6 over 794 hits' used as evidence for block charges; block charges stay as Canary's mechanic, but the clean data (33.6) sits closer to always-blocked; 2026-10-13 15:26 cyclops clear arena v4, the first clean comparison (full inventory restored before every run, forge off, same 250 ms action gate and 100 ms decision tick, heal below 160 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v4.tsv): Spiral rules 6/6 cleared, 87.9 +- 14.3 s, 14.7 +- 2.9 potions, 2471 +- 420 damage, 0 deaths; vBot 6/6, 90.0 +- 8.9 s, 14.8 +- 2.6 potions, 2486 +- 395, 0 deaths; a tie (Welch t -0.31 on time, -0.10 on potions), as the simulator expects for two threshold healers; next: the arena spot's terrain in the simulator, then a scenario where terrain or positioning separates policies; 2026-10-13 16:33 arena v5 (clean, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v5.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst) 7/7 cleared, 83.3 +- 6.3 s, 12.1 +- 2.8 potions, 2101 +- 432 damage; vBot 6/6, 83.4 +- 15.1 s, 13.0 +- 3.1, 2201 +- 469; Spiral rules 6/6, 83.1 +- 11.0 s, 14.2 +- 2.2, 2376 +- 337; no deaths; retreat uses the fewest potions at equal time, the simulator's direction, but smaller than predicted (-15% vs rules live, -33% in the simulator) and not yet significant (Welch t -1.45 vs rules, -0.52 vs vBot); 10 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 18:25 arena v5 final (16/16/15 runs, clean): Spiral retreat-at-2 13.8 +- 2.9 potions, 88.9 +- 9.9 s; vBot 14.1 +- 2.5, 88.0 +- 10.8 s; Spiral rules 14.4 +- 2.6, 86.8 +- 12.4 s; no deaths; no significant differences (retreat vs rules t -0.58); the early retreat advantage regressed to the mean; the simulator's ~30% saving does not transfer; live retreats mostly did not move the knight (sampled positions barely change): the probe left ChaseOpponent on, so the server walked the knight back toward its target; the probe now sets DontChase before each retreat step (diagnostic: 14 retreats, 3 positions, 12 potions); v6 (retreat vs rules, 8 rounds) running; 2026-10-13 19:11 arena v6 (retreat probe with DontChase, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 9/9 cleared, 13.3 +- 1.9 potions, 2281 +- 337 damage, 90.5 +- 8.3 s; Spiral rules 8/8, 15.0 +- 2.7 potions, 2566 +- 387, 90.2 +- 10.1 s; no deaths; 11% fewer potions and less damage at equal time, the simulator's direction at about a third of its predicted size (8.8 vs 12.4 per clear), not yet significant (Welch t -1.44, a retreat run beats a rules run in 68% of pairs); 8 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 19:57 arena v6 final (16-17 runs each, clean harness, heal 160): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 16/17 cleared, 88.4 +- 9.8 s, 13.1 potions on cleared runs, 2178 +- 491 damage taken; Spiral rules 16/16, 88.2 +- 11.8 s, 14.9 potions, 2544 +- 432 damage; no deaths; damage -14% (Welch t ~ -2.3), potions -13% (t -1.93; one-sided p ~0.03 for the direction the simulator predicted beforehand), equal clear time: the first live effect of a simulator-designed policy, about half the simulator's predicted size; one retreat run never cleared (it retreated out of the fight: 806 gate drops, no kills), a failure mode to handle (re-engage when no attacker is adjacent); 2026-10-13 20:39 arena v6 FINAL (23-24 runs each, clean harness, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv since 18:21): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 23/24 cleared, 12.6 potions on cleared runs, 2125 damage taken, 88.6 s; Spiral rules 23/23, 15.5 potions, 2639 damage, 91.7 s; no deaths; potions -19% (Welch t -3.89), damage -19% (t -4.20), clear time not different (t -0.96): the first statistically clear live win, for a policy the simulator found and evolution rediscovered (the simulator predicted -29%); vBot was at 14.1-14.8 potions in v4/v5 under the same harness, a head-to-head retreat vs vBot round is next; 2026-10-14 00:23 PAUSED at the user's request (account switch): arena v7 (retreat vs vBot, arena-results-cyclops-v7.tsv) stopped after 8 vBot and 7 retreat runs (retreat 11-15 potions, vBot 8-18; summarize with arena-summary.ps1); next on resume: finish v7, rescan the arena at radius 12 (probe-scan-body.lua, live knight leaves the +-7 window), mixed cyclops+troll camp probe (cavebot 240 potions/37.7 s vs evolved rules 431/43.5 s per 200 clears: rules tuned for cyclops lose on mixed camps); 2026-10-14 01:59 arena v7 final (retreat vs vBot, clean harness, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v7.tsv since 2026-10-13 23:30, 20 retreat / 21 vBot runs, all cleared, no deaths): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 12.1 sd 1.8 potions, 2083 sd 263 damage taken, 89.3 sd 10.3 s; vBot 13.8 sd 3.3 potions, 2371 sd 502 damage, 92.4 sd 13.4 s; potions -13% (Welch t -2.14, df 31, one-sided p 0.02), damage -12% (t -2.32, one-sided p 0.014), clear time not different (t -0.85): retreat beats vBot on supplies and damage at equal speed, smaller than its -19% margin over rules in v6; vBot is also less consistent (potion sd 3.3 vs 1.8); harness asymmetry found: probe-vbot-body.lua samples experience and health only every 10 s, so vBot clear times are rounded up to the next 10 s (about +5 s bias: corrected vBot clear 87.4 s, t +0.50, still no difference) and vBot lowest health is a 10 s sample, not a true minimum; the vBot probe now also watches every 100 ms for v8 on; v7 pools two policy snapshots (23:29 and 00:31) whose only difference is an additive Scored targeting case in policy.spi that live.spi does not use; 2026-10-14 02:18 arena spot rescanned at radius 12 (probe-scan-body.lua, tibia-local/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt: raw grid, 25 row bitmasks with bit i = column dx -12+i is #, and a client-loaded check): the knight was centered at 1933,1350 in that scan (one tile off the 1932,1349 reset; a second scan logged in at 1932,1349, so the knight's login tile varies run to run); the radius-12 scan cannot see past the client's loaded 18x14 window (x 1924..1941, y 1343..1356 in both scans): g_map.getTile returns nil outside it and the probe prints nil as #, so the outer band of solid # rows and columns is unknown terrain, not walls (probe-scan-unknown-body.lua prints ? there); a wider live map needs the knight to walk the area or a server-side or OTBM read, not a bigger client scan radius; inside the window the grid matches the radius-7 scan; 2026-10-14 03:24 arena v8 (heal below 120 for both, Spiral rules vs vBot, 10 runs each, arena-results-cyclops-v8.tsv since 2026-10-14 02:18, first round with the vBot probe watching experience and health every 100 ms): all 20 cleared, no deaths; Spiral rules 84.4 sd 6.0 s, 12.8 sd 1.6 potions, 2233 sd 235 damage, lowest health mean 67 (min 52); vBot 88.8 sd 16.0 s, 13.2 sd 3.7 potions, 2299 sd 572 damage, lowest mean 65 (min 28); no significant difference (Welch t -0.82 time, -0.31 potions, -0.34 damage); against heal 160 (v4-v7) both drink 1-2 fewer potions at equal damage and speed and run about 35-40 hp closer to death, still survivable with 3 cyclops; vBot stays the less consistent one (sd 3.7 potions, its two worst runs bottomed at 28 and 30 hp); earlier rounds' vBot lowest health (mean 169-192 at heal 160) was a 10 s sampling artifact, so vBot never had the larger safety margin those tables showed; 2026-10-14 03:32 vBot probe now stops at clear (100 ms watch, finish 'cleared', post-finish HealBot drinks not counted); smoke run cleared 93.7 s, 13 potions, lowest 109, log ends right after clear; 2026-10-14 04:43 arena v9 cyclops 12+12, retreat at 2, ReachFirst (spiral-retreat) vs CurrentFirst (spiral-retreat-current): potions 13.3+-2.6 vs 13.5+-3.4 (t -0.14), damage 2243+-373 vs 2290+-482 (t -0.27), clear 90.1+-9.0 vs 92.6+-11.8 s (t -0.59); all cleared, 0 deaths; no difference on the three metrics. Post-hoc: lowest health 91.6+-28.9 vs 113.1+-12.1 (t -2.38, two reach runs dipped to 34/36) - CurrentFirst never went below 93; 2026-10-14 04:59 arena v9 vBot reference (fixed probe, stops at clear, block after the Spiral runs, not interleaved) n=6: potions 14.0+-3.6, damage 2418+-575, clear 91.1+-9.9 s, 0 deaths; vs spiral-retreat t potions -0.40, damage -0.68, clear -0.21; vs spiral-retreat-current t -0.28, -0.47, +0.29 - no significant difference; vBot runs now ~2.8 min instead of ~3.8; 2026-10-14 05:51 arena v9 pooled (12 alternating + 6 interleaved with vBot, all cleared, 0 deaths): ReachFirst vs CurrentFirst n=18/18 potions 12.7+-2.3 vs 13.4+-3.2 (t -0.72), damage 2172+-326 vs 2263+-462 (t -0.68), clear 89.6+-9.1 vs 91.7+-11.3 s (t -0.61) - no difference, ReachFirst nominally ahead; lowest-health gap did not replicate (pooled 97.2 vs 109.2, t ~-1.6). vBot (fixed probe) n=12: potions 14.1+-3.2, damage 2397+-492, clear 90.7+-10.9; spiral-retreat vs vBot t potions -1.27, damage -1.39, clear -0.29 (interleaved-only n=6/6: potions t -2.06, damage t -1.80); 2026-10-14 05:53 all 12 v9 vBot logs end 'finish: cleared' (no run complete/timeout, 0 post-finish drinks); v8 vBot logs had 0 potions after clear either, so the old 150 s tail cost wall time only and did not bias v8 potions/damage. v9 95% CI ReachFirst-CurrentFirst: potions -0.7 [-2.6,+1.2], damage -91 [-363,+181], clear -2.1 s [-9.1,+4.9]; 2026-10-14 05:54 pooled verdict, retreat (ReachFirst) vs vBot over v7 and v9 (38 vs 33 runs, potions from server messages, unaffected by the old vBot sampling): 12.4 vs 13.9 potions, -11%, Welch t -2.36, same clear time; v9 alone (vBot via the fixed probe, 12 runs) t -1.27, so the effect is real but modest; damage pooled not quoted because log matching picked up extra vBot logs (44 logs vs 33 rows); targeting during retreats (ReachFirst vs CurrentFirst) is a wash live (18 each, |t| < 0.8); 2026-10-14 06:38 CORRECTION of the vBot claim: arena v10 (9 more pairs, 05:55-06:38, arena-results-cyclops-v10.tsv) went the other way (retreat 13.6 vs vBot 13.0 potions); pooled v7+v9+v10 (47 vs 42 runs): retreat 12.6 vs vBot 13.7 potions (-8.2%, Welch t -1.89, not significant), clear 90.7 vs 92.0 s, no deaths; the two rounds with identically measured probes (v9+v10) give t -0.75; verdict: the retreat policy is level with vBot, perhaps slightly better; it clearly beats our rules policy (-19%, t -3.89); the v7 result was a high draw that regressed; lesson: decide the run count before looking (sequential peeking inflated the first claim); 2026-10-14 08:37 nExBot prepared as the second open-source baseline: pinned at 19632d4 (v4.0.4, default branch head 2026-07-15; the benchmark table said pushed 2026-09-01, other branches), copied to tibia-local/bots/nExBot-19632d4 without git/tests/docs; its README links an MIT LICENSE file that is missing from the repo (matters for publication only); it ships an auto-updater and an analytics module that call GitHub and nexbot.cc, so tibia-local/bot-network-sandbox.lua stubs g_http, HTTP and g_platform.openUrl for every competitor (silent no-ops; the updater's no-HTTP fallback would open a browser); its HealBot compares every potion threshold against HP percent, even rules marked absolute HP, so parity with heal-below-160 is HP% 31 (about +-5 hp); probe-nexbot-body.lua selects config 'nExBot'; next, after PR-1 and PR-2: one live run to let it create its per-character UnifiedStorage, then seed HealBot.json, targetbot_configs/arena.json and the storage the way vBot is seeded", Feature, P1, D5, 85u32, Paused, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,benchmark", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_baselines () = Planning ("TIBIA-BASELINES", Minutes 2400u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:58Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 09:58 nExBot seeding prepared offline (read-only reading of nExBot 19632d4): HealBot.json in bot/nExBot/nExBot_configs/profile_{0,1}/ (same profile shape as vBot); the engine collapses HP and HP% into one hp threshold compared to floor(health*100/max) with <=, so heal below 160 at 515 max is hp% <= 30 (fires for health <= 159, exact); UnifiedStorage at nExBot_configs/characters/knight sample/UnifiedStorage.json (targetbot.enabled, selectedConfig arena, healbot.enabled), and vbot-arena.json is format-compatible (targeting/looting). The network sandbox is prepended to the runtime copy of _Loader.lua. Staged in run-policy-scenario.next.ps1 (-Bot nExBot) and run-arena.ps1 (competitor nexbot); swapped in after PR-1. Earlier note said 31%: that was wrong (floor semantics).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 2u32, "2026-10-14T14:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 10:30 CORRECTION: every live spiral-* run since 2026-10-13 11:48 ran with vBot's HealBot and TargetBot active alongside our policy (the vBot probe enabled the client's bot setting for the character; nothing reset it; the policy probe never disabled it). Signature: server-reported potions our policy never drank in almost every spiral run (tibia-local/harness-check.ps1 scans all logs). All live policy comparisons and the live check of the simulator's clear prediction are therefore hybrids; PR-1 is void and stopped at 61 rows. Fix: run-policy-scenario writes the bot node per competitor and removes other bots' folders, the policy probe disables the bot before login, and run-arena records foreign potions/actions per run. Re-measurement: BENCHMARK PR-4. Server-mechanics fidelity rows and the 10-13 03:34 troll targeting run are unaffected.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 3u32, "2026-10-14T18:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 14:53 PR-4 (fixed harness, 30 runs each, 0 harness failures, 0 deaths): potions rules 11.53, retreat 12.90, vBot 14.00; retreat vs vBot difference -1.10 (CI -2.62 .. 0.42, t -1.45) no difference shown; retreat vs rules +1.37 (t 1.82) no difference shown, direction against retreat. Clear times 87.6 / 91.3 / 92.7 s match the simulator's 88.6 / 88.1; potions do not (predicted 13.23 rules, 9.09 retreat; t -3.69 and 6.44). The live retreat win and the 'simulator predicts live' claim from the hybrid runs are withdrawn.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 4u32, "2026-10-14T20:31Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:31 live random control (PR-5, probe-random-body.lua, 10 runs, clean): 94.1 potions per clear (simulator 90.5, holds), 102.7 s (simulator 117.0, gap: live auto-attack persists between random picks). Control far below rules 11.5, retreat 12.9, vBot 14.0.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 5u32, "2026-10-14T20:33Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:33 nExBot: 3/3 PR-3 check runs crash the client (TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH); PR-3 not run today.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 6u32, "2026-10-15T07:06Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 03:06 PR-8 (pre-registered replication, rules vs vBot, 30 each, clean): 12.90 vs 14.17 potions, difference -1.27 (CI -2.99 .. 0.46), t -1.47: no difference shown; PR-4's descriptive 11.53 for rules did not replicate. Both Spiral policies sit ~1.2 potions below vBot without significance at n=30.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 7u32, "2026-10-15T10:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 05:50: nExBot 4.0.4 is now a running baseline (three harness shims, BENCHMARK PR-3a). Pre-registered results on the clean harness: retreat vs vBot no difference shown (PR-4, t -1.45), rules vs vBot no difference shown (PR-8, t -1.47), retreat vs nExBot significant (PR-3a, 12.2 vs 14.6 potions, t -2.14, narrow). Left: OTCv8 bot module, scripted cavebot as a live competitor.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 8u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: open parts: OTCv8 bot module, scripted cavebot as a live competitor, and nExBot's license (see TIBIA-ARENA-RELEASE).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 9u32, "2026-10-15T11:04Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:04 correction: nExBot's license is not a task (no interaction with public projects); open parts are the OTCv8 bot module and a scripted cavebot as a live competitor.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 10u32, "2026-10-15T16:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 12:54 PR-9 (pre-registered 08:13, 50 runs each): Spiral rules 12.46 vs vBot 14.66 potions per cyclops clear, diff -2.20 (CI -3.35..-1.05), Welch t -3.80: SIGNIFICANT, rules use fewer potions; same clear time (88.7 vs 87.9 s), 0 deaths, damage 2145 vs 2479 (the saving is damage avoided). First well-powered live win over an open-source baseline. One disclosed interim look at 10:37 (fixed n, no early stop).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 11u32, "2026-10-15T18:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 14:14 PR-9 explained (post-hoc): the whole rules-vs-vBot difference is the knight's login protection. Canary ends it on the player's own move/autowalk/turn/say/item use/attack cancel, not on starting an attack; our probe keeps it, vBot ends it. Hits in the first 10 s: vBot 9.14, rules 1.58; after 10 s level (60.1 vs 60.4). So PR-9 measures a scenario artifact, not hunting skill. Harness fix next: end the protection for every competitor right after login (one native turn outside the parity gate), then re-test rules vs vBot (PR-11).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 12u32, "2026-10-15T22:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:40 PR-11 (pre-registered 14:21; parity.lua now ends login protection for every competitor with one native turn after login): rules 14.42 vs vBot 14.78 potions, diff -0.36 (CI -1.58..0.86), t -0.58: NO DIFFERENCE SHOWN; hits 69.1 vs 69.2, first 10 s 9.6 vs 9.0, clear 88.3 vs 87.4 s, 0 deaths. Our rules policy and vBot are level; PR-9's win was the login-protection artifact. Next for a real win: a behavior that changes exposure live (the model's policy effects are too strong, PR-10), not thresholds.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 13u32, "2026-10-15T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:49 remaining harness asymmetry after the protection fix: parity.lua ends login protection at 0.3 s for everyone, but the policy probe starts deciding about 2.5 s after login while vBot acts at once (PR-11 first-10-s hits 9.6 vs 9.0, consistent). Does not change PR-11's no-difference verdict; a test for a win should start every competitor's logic at the same moment. Recorded in BENCHMARK.md Parity.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 14u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 paused (user). On resume: TIBIA-START-SYNC, then run the written PR-12 (fair nExBot re-test); the OTCv8 module and a scripted live cavebot stay open.")
