inl note_of_tibia_storage_boundary_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-STORAGE-BOUNDARY", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: the compiler lane's WGSL parallel lanes (one seed per thread, chunked dispatch, pack-1e) already run gpu_sim with scratch arrays bit-exact, so the boundary is no longer blocking; lowered to P3 until a second GPU workload needs it.")
inl tibia_headless_client () = Task ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", "Headless game client in Spiral (Rust target) for agents and the arena harness: Canary 3.6.1 keeps the classic login protocol on loginProtocolPort 7171 (raw RSA private exponentiation over a 128-byte block with the datapack key.pem, then XTEA with the client key and Adler-32 checksums, src/server/network/protocol/protocollogin.cpp:125-135), so no HTTP login service is needed; allowOldProtocol=false; Canary accepts exactly CLIENT_VERSION 1511 (src/core.hpp:18), or 11.00 when allowOldProtocol is set; per-agent typed view (15x11 tiles) as the only observation; action-rate cap enforced at the protocol layer for parity; 2026-10-13 02:44 user: keep harnessing OTClient to the end (the baseline bots run as Lua inside it, and Spiral's Lua backend can run our policy there too); deferred until many parallel sessions are actually needed", Feature, P4, D6, 0u32, Paused, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD,SPIRAL-BIGNUM-MODEXP,TIBIA-TCP-BYTES", "tibia,protocol", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_headless_client () = Planning ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", Minutes 1800u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_headless_client_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: still deferred (user 2026-10-13: harness OTClient to the end); the OTClient harness now runs three competitors and two baselines, so there is no pressure to resume.")
inl tibia_oracle_rng () = Task ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", "Canary draws every random number from one global std::mt19937 seeded by std::random_device (src/utils/tools.cpp:449 getRandomGenerator; uniform_random/normal_random/boolean_random, 110 call sites in 18 files: combat.cpp 16, monster.cpp 17, game.cpp 13, ...); std::uniform_int_distribution is implementation-defined (MSVC and libstdc++ differ), so no simulator RNG can match it bit for bit: fidelity for RNG mechanics is distributional (sample each formula, compare with a goodness-of-fit test), and only deterministic mechanics are diffed exactly; a seed override (env var) in a locally built Canary still helps reproduce single scenarios; the C++ build is heavy (vcpkg), schedule it through the gate", TaskKind, P3, D4, 0u32, Paused, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,oracle,canary", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_oracle_rng () = Planning ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", Minutes 300u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_oracle_rng_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: re-checked against the local source: getRandomGenerator is still tools.cpp:449 in Canary 3.6.1. Distribution tests (PR-style) have replaced exact RNG diffs in practice; lowered to P3.")
inl tibia_numeric_standard () = Task ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", "Server formulas computed in double are reimplemented as exact integer arithmetic so they stay bit-exact on CPU and on WGSL (no f64 there): first case 2026-10-12, Canary Weapons::getMaxWeaponDamage melee offensive std::round(0.085 * attackFactor * attackValue * attackSkill + level / 5) == (85*v*s*2 + 1000) / 2000 + level / 5 for every (value 1..120 step 7, skill 10..130 step 3, level 1/8/100/777) case, 2,788 combinations, 0 differences against a PowerShell double reference (apps/tibia/damage.spi); attackFactor is a float (1.2f is not 1.2), so balanced/defensive modes need the exact binary value of the factor as a rational and a sweep before use; overflow budget: products stay inside i32 for attack <= 200 and skill <= 150, larger formulas need u64 emulation on WGSL", Story, P1, D4, 90u32, Paused, "TIBIA-STANDARDS", "tibia,standards,wgsl", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_numeric_standard () = Planning ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_numeric_standard_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: the only float left in apps/tibia is creatures.spi:37, Canary's step-speed formula 857.36*log(speed+261.29)-4795.01 in f64 (not WGSL-safe). Next: replace with an exact integer table over the speeds the arena uses, with a test against the f64 values.")
inl note_of_tibia_numeric_standard_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", 2u32, "2026-10-15T11:11Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:11 creatures.spi: canary_step_speed is now exact integer arithmetic (19 linear pieces over /4096, products < 5e6), equal to Canary's double formula for every speed 1..408 (canary_step_speed_exact_up_to; C test integer_step_speed_equals_canary_double_formula_for_every_speed_up_to_its_exact_limit, WGSL row integer_step_speed_on_gpu; creatures 8/8). The double formula survives only as that test's oracle. Melee max (damage.spi) replayed against Canary's doubles in Python over attack 1..200 x skill 1..150 x 3 modes x 5 levels: 450000 cases, 19 differ, all balanced-mode .5 ties where 0.085*0.75f in double lands just below (7 attack/skill pairs, attack 20/40/80 with skill 100/50/90/25/45/85/95); the simulated weapons (21/60, 20/30) never tie. Left: pin those tie pairs if a scenario ever uses them.")
inl kino_shared_daemon_queue () = Task ("KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", "Every lane and session talks to one compile daemon on port 13905, which serializes compiles: concurrent Kino runs from different sessions queue behind each other (2026-10-12: two math runs waited ~20 min with no compiles logged while clients waited); options: per-session ports by default (SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER_PORT already exists), a daemon pool sized by free memory, or fair queuing per client; measure with xsim (several BEAMs sharing one daemon) before and after; user decision 2026-10-13 07:08: no model chosen up front; experiment with each (per-session ports, a memory-sized pool with fair queuing, one daemon with round-robin) under xsim load (several BEAMs, multiple lanes) and keep iterating until state of the art; measure wait time, throughput, peak memory per model; 2026-10-13 12:15 Kino lane measured four models with a load harness (3 BEAM sessions x 6 lib compiles, 3 in flight each, warm daemons, 2 rounds, machine shared with other lanes): one FIFO daemon 60-69 s wall, 0.26-0.30/s, queue p50 26.5 s, peak compiler 575-647 MB; per-session ports 44-48 s, 0.38-0.41/s, queue p50 9.6-13.3 s, peak 1.0-1.2 GB (plus a cold daemon per session); pool of 3 fair 41.3 s, 0.44/s, queue p50 9.8 s p95 13.1 s, peak 1.1 GB when memory allowed growth (round 2 under a parallel lib sweep stayed at 1 compiler by the free-memory gate: 103 s); round-robin on 1 compiler 54-87 s; unequal sessions (12 vs 2 vs 2 requests): light sessions finish at 12-17 s under FIFO and fair alike (a session never has more than its own concurrency in flight), fair finished the heavy one 4-12 s earlier; decision: one daemon with a memory-sized pool (up to 3 compilers, a new one only when free memory >= SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_SERVER_MB 1000 + SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_RESERVE_MB 1500) and fair per-client queues, now the default (SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_POOL=off|N|auto); per-worker recycle cap = max(2500/workers, 1200) MB; retire waits for queued and running pool compiles and stops the extra compilers; clients send their OS pid as the client id; tests in compiler_pool_test.exs; 2026-10-13 12:19 end-to-end with the default (pool auto): 18/18 in 49 s, 0.37/s, queue p50 10.5 s, peak 1.09 GB (grew to 3 compilers at 4.6-5.5 GB free); retire stopped all 3 compilers (no orphans)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY", "kino,perf,daemon", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_shared_daemon_queue () = Planning ("KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kino_shared_daemon_queue_1 () = Note ("KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", 1u32, "2026-10-16T03:11Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 23:11 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) the xsim measurements now live in the i574n/x repo (apps/sim). Kino test runs from a sibling repo work with SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER=process (no daemon left behind).")
inl kino_memo_key_scope () = Task ("KINO-MEMO-KEY-SCOPE", "Memo key scope (tibia lane measurement 2026-10-12: second pass mostly missed): package prints by size+mtime of every .spi in an included dir and an md5 of every Kino module invalidated far too much; 17:30 Kino lane, in apps/kino memo.ex (uncommitted): a package enters the key as sha256 of package.spiproj + content of exactly the listed modules (folder entries + children, .spi and .spir) + path dependencies recursively, test blocks included (correctness first), core package the same way; unlisted files/size/mtime no longer matter; Kino identity = md5 of result-path modules only (Spiral.Kino, Builders, Cell, Directives, Display, Domain + Gleam domain beam, Memo, Mounts, Notebook, Result, Runner, Targets, Toolchain), excluding SmartCell, Document, CompilerClient/Daemon, Fsi*, Slots, FileLock, mix tasks; memo_test.exs covers unlisted-file edit keeps the key, listed module/folder module/project edit changes it; entries written before miss once; correction: the landing note above is from 17:14, not 17:30; verified by the tibia lane (port 13935): fill hunt 36.2 s / hunt_sim 27.3 s; touching the unlisted wire.spi (content + mtime) -> hunt 6.8 s memo_hits 4/4, hunt_sim 6.4 s 5/5; touching the listed geometry.spi (trailing newline) -> hunt memo_hits 0, 33.2 s; whitespace-only edits invalidate (safe; a token-level hash is a possible later refinement)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,perf,memo", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_memo_key_scope () = Planning ("KINO-MEMO-KEY-SCOPE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kino_memo_key_scope_1 () = Note ("KINO-MEMO-KEY-SCOPE", 1u32, "2026-10-14T23:20Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 19:20 Tibia lane observation: apps/tibia/pack_sim.spi reported 22 memo hits of 24 right after hunting_pack.spi (a module the tests open) gained a new function, so the memo key seems to leave out the content of opened package modules; a test whose own text is unchanged could pass from memo after its dependency changed behavior. Today's SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0 rerun was also 24/24, so no wrong pass here. Worth checking whether dependency modules are part of the key.")
inl kino_not_run_reason () = Task ("KINO-NOT-RUN-REASON", "When a test in a --test list fails, later tests are reported not_run (fail-fast) without saying why; the report row should carry the reason (e.g. \"not_run: stopped after <test> failed\") (tibia lane, 2026-10-12); 20:46 done (uncommitted): every not_run row carries reason: 'the run stopped before this test: <first line of the error>' or 'no step ran for this cell'", TaskKind, P3, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,report", "current", "current")
