inl tibia_canary_pitfalls () = Task ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", "Canary setup pitfalls found 2026-10-12: scoop lua51 sets LUA_PATH/LUA_CPATH, which override Canary's require paths (\"no field package.preload['data-otservbr-global.lib.core.quests']\"), so clear them for canary.exe (tibia-local/world.ps1 does); the release zip holds only canary.exe/pdb, the datapack comes from the v3.6.1 source tag; the global datapack (otservbr.otbm, 176 MB) needs well over 1.2 GB while loading, the small data-canary datapack (canary.otbm 18.8 MB, 67 monster types, no rat, no spawns) starts in 30 s at 112 MB and suits arena scenarios that define their own spawns; /m on the player's own tile fails in the temple (\"There is not enough room\"), the radius form /m name,count,,radius places monsters around; experience stayed 4200 after a kill because data-canary green_frog.lua sets monster.experience = 0; its targetDistance = 6 makes it keep six tiles away, which looked like fleeing in the probes (health 25, melee 0..25 every 2000 ms before armor, observed hits 2..12): pick arena creatures with targetDistance 1 and non-zero experience, and treat each creature's Lua definition as the oracle for the simulator's creature table", TaskKind, P3, D1, 0u32, Paused, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,canary", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls () = Planning ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: new pitfalls from 2026-10-15: (1) any follow packet clears the player's attack target without telling the client (Game::playerFollowCreature); (2) with classicAttackSpeed=false a player step cancels the scheduled swing (Player::onWalk, PC-3); (3) OTClient Redemption crashes (0xC0000374) on native nested dofile and on errors under pcall around it in the bot sandbox; (4) a scenario exception leaves canary.exe running and run-arena hangs on the inherited pipe.")
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 2u32, "2026-10-15T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:49 biggest pitfall of the day, login protection: Canary 3.6.1 keeps monsters off a fresh login for 10 s (loginProtectionTime) and ends it on the player's own move, auto-walk, turn, speech, item use or attack cancel (Game::playerMove/playerAutoWalk/playerTurn/playerSay/playerUseItem*/playerSetAttackedCreature with id 0); starting an attack does not. A probe that only attacks keeps it, bots that turn or talk lose it, and the difference decided PR-9. Harness now ends it for everyone (parity.lua).")
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 3u32, "2026-10-15T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:49 ramps: stepping onto a tile whose item has a floorchange direction (e.g. item 6913 'ramp', floorchange south at 1940,1372,7) moves the walker one floor up and one tile on (to 1940,1373,6); monsters only target players on their own floor, so a retreat onto a ramp ends the fight. otbm-walkability.py --items-xml/--floor-changes lists such tiles; mind self-closing <item/> tags when parsing items.xml.")
inl tibia_fidelity_walk () = Task ("TIBIA-FIDELITY-WALK", "First oracle-backed test: apps/tibia/geometry.spi steps_match_canary_walk_probe_2026_10_12 pins the server-confirmed positions of a N/E/S/W walk from (1942, 1346, 7) (north y-1, east x+1, south y+1, west x-1); run it once Kino is available again; collect more probe traces (diagonal steps, floor changes, blocked tiles) the same way; 2026-10-13 06:14 N/E/S/W and diagonal steps pinned from server-confirmed probes (geometry.spi); floor changes and blocked tiles not yet measured", TaskKind, P2, D1, 80u32, Paused, "TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", "tibia,oracle", "current", "current")
