inl kino_gleam_false_pass () = Task ("KINO-GLEAM-FALSE-PASS", "Found and fixed 21:16 by the Kino lane (uncommitted): ///> gleam (erlang target, the default) never ran a test's program, so every gleam test passed regardless of its asserts: Kino wrote main.gleam into the cell dir, the spiral CLI's process_gleam treats the source dir's parent as the package dir, so it wrote gleam.toml into the shared %TEMP%/spiral_kino and gleam run failed there (exit 1, stderr dropped) while the CLI still exited 0 with empty output; repro test gleam_fails = 1i32 |> _assert_eq 2i32 reported passed; fix: gleam output goes to <cell>/gleam/src/main.gleam and Kino itself writes gleam.toml (CLI dependency list + the cell's -d deps), runs gleam build then gleam run and uses their exit codes (missing gleam = unsupported; -t javascript still via the CLI); verified: gleam_fails fails with the __assert_eq panic, gleam_passes passes with plain output (agreement can now compare gleam); ~16 s per gleam test (dependencies compiled per cell); every earlier passed gleam target in lib runs was unverified", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,gleam,false-pass", "current", "current")
