inl note_of_bundler_debug_stack_overflow_6 () = Note ("BUNDLER-DEBUG-STACK-OVERFLOW", 6u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: fix verified on the candidate: host-compile-stack.ps1 runs the positional compileOne on a 1 GB-stack thread; a Debug single-flight build compiles typecheck_long_let_body (C 6 s, F# 11 s; was 0xC00000FD in 2 s), and Debug, Release and the committed main.c / main.fsx are byte-identical. Lands with PACK-NIGHT-1017. Pack: night pack 10-17 (scripts %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\packs\\night-1017, each with -DryRun; final review single-flight-20261017-053315 on the exact pack: 6,906 rows, DISAGREE 0, residual-only Zig 457 and Rust 415, 3 intended Rust exit cells (shown as 2 NATIVE-DIFF rows); builds in single-flight, hopacsota and gpt5parallel; hopacsota inline and random:23 equal single-flight on every compile and residual cell; corpus 144 of 144; Zig at C speed on the bench).")
inl note_of_bundler_debug_stack_overflow_7 () = Note ("BUNDLER-DEBUG-STACK-OVERFLOW", 7u32, "2026-10-17T18:24Z", "bundle-wisdom", "14:24 from the bundles: (a) bootstrap_llm_compiler_v69/v71 (2026-01-04): List.fold/List.map and small let rec loops over AST lists inside the evaluator (ERecordWith, ERecordTest) overflowed before any guard ran. The canonical patch was an explicit while loop (descent with a parent stack, then bottom-up rebuild) with a periodic EnsureSufficientExecutionStack checkpoint. Checklist: if ListModule.Fold/Map frames show up in the trace, the library recursion is the culprit, not term. (b) brzozowski alpha54 (Sep 2026): turning proof-only let rec into inl rec over a runtime recursive union stack-overflowed the F# prepass; making the runtime loops local let rec (staged through a join point) fixed it. The ask was a diagnostic naming the unbounded inline recursion and its source span instead of a raw stack overflow.")
