inl kino_default_target () = Task ("KINO-DEFAULT-TARGET", "2026-10-13 07:28 an untargeted test block or a file's 'test x static' prelude compiles Rust (Builders.default = blank(:rust)); user: 'rust is slow to compile, we need a reason for having such cells'; make the default target configurable per package or file (apps/tibia wants c) and stop compiling the static prelude cell natively; serves: fast Tibia iterations; 2026-10-13 08:45 done: untargeted tests use the ///> lines of the file's static prelude test (///> c above test x static =), else SPIRAL_KINO_DEFAULT_TARGET / default_target:, else Rust host; static preludes are never compiled or run (row status static, own count, not executed); real run: default_fixture with ///> c prelude ran its test on c (passed), prelude static; tests in notebook_report_test.exs, notebook_test.exs updated; README", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,tibia,performance", "current", "current")
inl kino_one_front_end_per_test () = Task ("KINO-ONE-FRONT-END-PER-TEST", "2026-10-13 07:28 measured on apps/tibia (per-target ms): rust avg 10.5 s (max 22.5), c 8.2 s, wgsl 7.5 s, lua 6.4 s per test; C's time is mostly the Spiral compile, not gcc, and each extra ///> target repeats the whole front end and partial evaluation; partial-evaluate once per test and emit every listed backend from that result, so an extra target costs only its codegen and native build; serves: multi-target tests (c oracle + wgsl GPU + lua live) without multiplying compile time; 2026-10-13 09:51 Kino lane measurement (apps/tibia damage.spi, 3 c tests + 1 wgsl, warm daemon, memo off): every unit-ending test compiled twice (attempt 1 failed main : i32 = <unit>, then the 0i32 retry; daemon log error+change per test); fix: scoped test bodies ending in an _assert call emit spiral_kino_test () then 0i32, so one compile; per-test 11.8-15.7 s -> 5.6-8.7 s, Kino compile phase 3.4-6.0 s -> 2.8-3.0 s, server compile ~0.7-0.9 s per test; 2026-10-13 12:24 final (damage.spi, 3 c + 1 wgsl, warm, memo off, pool default): per test 3.9-4.0 s (from 11.8-15.7 s this morning), whole file 15 s wall (from 40 s); phases now compile 0.8-2.0 s, queue 0.4-2.0 s, target (gcc -O2 + run) 0.9-1.3 s, mount 8-20 ms, cleanup 3-28 ms, so Kino's own overhead is gone; a second ///> target of the same test is already a front-end hit ('compile unchanged' in the daemon log: the server reuses parse/typecheck for the unchanged file and only partial-evaluates and generates for the new backend, ~1-1.6 s), and partial evaluation is backend-specific, so no further sharing is possible there", Feature, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,compiler,tests,performance", "current", "current")
inl tibia_cooldown_per_spell () = Task ("TIBIA-COOLDOWN-PER-SPELL", "2026-10-13 08:03 found by the new GADT readiness test (apps/tibia/readiness.spi): cooldowns.spi kept one shared spell_ready_at, so any spell's own cooldown blocked every other spell (a heal right after a strike was refused); Canary keeps the own cooldown per spell id (spells.cpp: CONDITION_SPELLCOOLDOWN with m_spellId) and group cooldowns per group; fixed: spell carries spell_id, timers hold strike/light_healing/haste own slots plus the three group slots; the old test own_cooldown_gates_every_group pinned the wrong belief and became own_cooldown_gates_only_the_same_spell_like_canary; sims re-pinned: standing scripted seed 7 now 0 kills / 10 escapes (its earlier kill came from the bug), hunter_survives_and_kills restated for the chasing cavebot, chasing 357 vs standing 27 kills, pack CurrentFirst 360 vs ReachFirst 59", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,fidelity,cooldowns", "current", "current")
inl tibia_typed_domain () = Task ("TIBIA-TYPED-DOMAIN", "2026-10-13 08:07 user priority: domain modeling with GADTs, existentials and HKTs instead of the PhantomData simulation used in the Rust apps; first four apps/tibia modules, each with negative tests (programs that must not compile) and C + WGSL rows: quantity.spi (phantom units: amount hitpoints/milliseconds/tiles/gold_coins; hp + ms and gold-as-health fail), readiness.spi (GADT witnesses: ready attack_group / ready healing_group, gates open only when the group and spell are ready, Strike needs an attack proof; its first run exposed TIBIA-COOLDOWN-PER-SPELL), catalog.spi (existential spawn catalog: kind k GADT over troll/goblin/cyclops tags, entry = exists k. spawn k, a troll spawn cannot hold a cyclops), views.spi (HKT: prototype mapped f with instances one and lanes, decide_all written once over f : * -> *, a view without mapped is rejected); next: wire them into the simulators (mixed packs from the catalog, strikes gated by readiness proofs, units through hunt state), then the lanes view for batched GPU evaluation; limitation: constructors are public, so a witness can be forged by calling the constructor directly (needs module-private constructors); 2026-10-13 08:13 wired in: pack_sim now runs a camp of three kinds (existential catalog entries unpacked by catalog.entry_creature; the all-troll numbers are unchanged, a mixed troll/goblin/troll camp gets 357 kills over 20 seeds), strikes require a readiness.ready attack_group proof (a bare timestamp is rejected), the player's health is quantity.amount hitpoints through the whole state; finding: record update is structural, so {p with player_health = quantity.ms 150} type-checks and makes a new record type; the unit error only appears where a pack is expected (respawn_player), so state that must keep its field types should be a nominal, not a type alias; 2026-10-13 08:52 vocations.spi: spell v GADT indexed by vocation tags (knight, paladin, sorcerer, druid); single-vocation spells are typed by their vocation (WoundCleansing, Berserk : spell knight; DivineHealing : spell paladin), shared spells need a healer v proof (LightHealing, IntenseHealing), and no knight healer exists, so a knight casting exura is a compile error; data from Canary's spell scripts (words, level, mana, cooldowns, group); found: the simulators' knight was casting Light Healing, which knights cannot cast; it now casts Wound Cleansing (same 1 s / 1 s cooldowns, own cooldown slot WoundCleansingSpell), all pinned numbers unchanged; package order matters (a module sees only earlier modules), so vocations sits before readiness; 2026-10-13 16:58 afternoon additions, all bit-exact refactors or new rules with negative tests: readiness gains an action-slot witness (ready action_slot from the 250 ms parity gate; potions and retreat steps need it; an attack proof cannot pay for one); the objective is a unit-indexed GADT (Kills :: objective kill_score, Profit/ProfitKeepingKills/CheapClearWithin :: objective gold_coins, measured returns amount unit; kills_and_gold_do_not_add fails to compile); network weights are addressed through feature/output unions and a hidden nominal (an output passed as a feature fails); terrain is a layout union with a pure integer blocked function (the scanned arena spot as row masks, so WGSL works); combat has a typed gear record from Canary's formula; views gains a trio container and a counted HKT prototype (instances for one, lanes and trio), and the pack now holds its foes as views.trio with attacker counts and occupancy as counted folds; quantity gains scaled; gold and potion costs are amount gold_coins; next: module-private constructors (SPIRAL-PRIVATE-CONSTRUCTORS) so witnesses cannot be forged; 2026-10-14 07:35 GPU: new notebook apps/tibia/gpu_sim.spi pairs C and WGSL runs of the multi-creature simulator: 10 ticks, a full 3000-tick troll hunt and 20 arena-spot cyclops clears are bit-exact on WGSL (4/4 green); throughput waits on WGSL-PARALLEL-LANES (single-thread dispatch today); 2026-10-14 07:44 the benchmark protocol is now type-checked: hunting_pack gains role-indexed seed blocks (nominal training, held_out; union seed_block role = TrainingBlock :: seed_range -> seed_block training | HeldOutBlock :: seed_range -> seed_block held_out) and typed entry points (cavebot_heal_tuned_on, rules_evolved_on, tactic_evolved_on, worth_on_training take only training blocks; judged_on, clears_judged_on only held-out blocks; ledger_on either); every benchmark test in pack_sim migrated (no raw seed ranges left), all 20 tests green with unchanged pins; tuning on held-out seeds and judging on training seeds are compile-time failures (two negative tests)", Feature, P1, D5, 80u32, Paused, "", "tibia,modeling,gadt,existential,hkt", "current", "current")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_domain_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-DOMAIN", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: new typed rule today: union swing_after_step (SwingKeepsItsTime | SwingWaitsForThink) as a camp field, default-off so earlier pins are untouched.")
