inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_3 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 3u32, "2026-10-14T08:56Z", "lane 2", "proof: on a copy of this backlog two notes (quotes and a backslash round-trip), from-title on HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH moved 15 notes (title 2,099 -> 108 bytes), agile check build_attested=2 on the copy; tests src/eoie_contracts/tests/agile_note_receipts.rs 4/4 (whole receipt lines, show text and JSON, rejections leave state byte-identical, concurrent writer), with agile_receipts and proxy_receipts 10/10 against src/target/debug/eoie.exe; dev.ps1 on the 10 packages: 10/10 emitted, cargo check ok, package tests ok except eoie-contracts lib expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface (failed once under load at 232 s; passes alone with the same dev-validation binary and with the deployed one); real backlog: these notes, agile check build_attested=2; left: deploy the new eoie.exe (the deployed one does not print notes), renew owner growth and strict evidence (compiler-contracts/renew-strict-evidence.ps1), migrate long titles with notes from-title when their lanes are idle")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_4 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 4u32, "2026-10-14T09:20Z", "lane 2", "review round: the after-read test pause now writes state/agile.spi.paused so the concurrent-writer test waits for the marker instead of a fixed sleep; new test an_expired_lease_blocks_note_from_title_and_rename_alike (expired prompt.spi lease, no lease policy): note, notes from-title and rename are all refused with 'lease authority blocked mutating effect' and leave the state byte-identical, so the from-title root position does not bypass the lease; agile_note_receipts 5/5; eoie-contracts lib suite 8/8 (7 ignored) in the tree against the deployed eoie.exe (14 s), the new debug build (132 s) and dev.ps1's dev-validation build (108 s); dev.ps1 -Package <the 10 packages> emitted 10/10 and passed cargo check and every package test except eoie-contracts lib expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface, which failed in both staged runs (239 s) although the same binaries pass it in the tree: cause not found, next: dev.ps1 -Package eoie-contracts on a clean checkout to see whether it predates this change")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_5 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 5u32, "2026-10-14T09:24Z", "lane 2", "staged-only lease failure explained: eoie-contracts lib expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface clears EOIE_LEASE_POLICY but not EOIE_LEASE_ROOT (contracts.rs:158, from contracts_entry/harness.spi), and an inherited EOIE_LEASE_ROOT pointing at a live lease reproduces the failure in the tree with the same dev-validation binary (fails in 0.07 s; passes without it), so it is a pre-existing test fragility of the staged dev workflow, not this change; fix: env_remove(EOIE_LEASE_ROOT) in that test's commands (needs contracts.rs regeneration); topology after this batch: topology_limits_ok=true, cargo_crate_count=134 (was 128), rust_global_site_count=261 (unchanged), largest crate 995 lines (rust_std_fs_mutation); the round-2 edits (pause marker, rename guards) were compiled directly with the same compiler and not yet compared with a staged regeneration")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_6 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 6u32, "2026-10-14T10:01Z", "lane 2", "deployed: eoie build.ps1 (release 3m33s, schema and source-topology checks) published the repo-root eoie.exe (sha256 DD36D652D7AB.. -> 44897B5C8234..); this deployed binary prints these notes under the title (agile show) and as a 5-entry notes array (--json), and agile check on this backlog passes (build_attested=1); before that eoie dev.ps1 -Package on the 11 affected packages -Publish passed end to end (719 s, 0 owners changed): eoie-contracts lib 8/8 incl. the lease test, agile_note_receipts 6/6, agile_receipts 1/1, proxy_receipts 5/5, batch_completion 2/2; the earlier staged-only lease failure came from contracts.rs being hand-patched in a743a92 without its source contracts_entry/harness.spi, now carried in the source (plus env_remove EOIE_LEASE_ROOT); note the release also contains the other lane's uncommitted proxy_failure_classification/eoie_proxy_edit_contracts edits; not done: compiler-contracts/renew-strict-evidence.ps1 (build.ps1 -Test -CompilerContracts on the whole workspace, cold rebuild of every chain, release-closeout apply), which would take well over the remaining time and bake the other lane's uncommitted edits into evidence: run it after both lanes commit")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_body_7 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-BODY", 7u32, "2026-10-14T13:24Z", "lane-b", "dogfood finding (on a copy, not applied): notes from-title SOCIAL-TRANSPORT-SIM moved 95 fragments: it cuts at every '; ', so the title ends mid-parenthesis ('...(user 2026-10-12: deferring it was a bad call') and undated clauses become separate 'migrated' notes; fix: split only before a dated segment ('; yyyy-MM-dd' or '; HH:mm'), keep undated clauses with the previous note. Renewal for both items running (lane B, through the gate)")
