inl harness_agree_fail () = Task ("HARNESS-AGREE-FAIL", "Harness classifier hides wrong answers (found 2026-10-14 03:02 by the research lane, confirmed at apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/test.ps1:619): agree-fail treats any two nonzero exits as a shared failure, so a sample whose main returns a value (42, 235) reports a backend's wrong answer as agreement; 90 C rows exit nonzero, exposing 460 non-C rows; currently masking lua_while_union_pair [Wasm] (1 vs 235: wasmtime 39 proc_exit rejects statuses >= 126); fix: agree-fail only when both exits are failure-class; companions H2 (bless keeps 55 stale rows for backends no longer scheduled), H3 (abi_external_buffer_length_negative has no C-flags rule, its C row is a link failure), H4 (c-only label can mask a ran-but-different row); patch scripts in the job scratch after-bless/; apply after tonight's bless, then rerun -Suite all -Native and review every row that flips", Story, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,harness,correctness", "current", "current")
inl note_of_harness_agree_fail_1 () = Note ("HARNESS-AGREE-FAIL", 1u32, "2026-10-14T10:39Z", "user", "2026-10-14 06:39 user decision: apply the after-bless fix scripts now (on top of tonight's blessed oracle), not after pack 2, in RUNBOOK.md order, then rerun -Suite all -Native single-flight, review every flipped row and rebless once; gpt5parallel no longer gates the bless")
