inl note_of_harness_agree_fail_5 () = Note ("HARNESS-AGREE-FAIL", 5u32, "2026-10-14T13:54Z", "main-thread", "09:54 the first -Bless run (single-flight-20261014-083026) was spoiled and blessed anyway (DISAGREE 6). Cause, my error: the R4 policy suite (night cache, R4 DLL built from source that already had the WGSL lanes edits) started at 09:47 on the same sample tree. test.ps1's mutex is per cache dir and outputs compile in place, so it overwrote main.wgsl/.c/.rs mid-run. Result: 4 Wgsl residuals hashed foreign output, plus 6 native timeouts (new shaders on the old runner; load). R4 stopped, other heavy jobs held, lanes asked to keep the gate free; a clean -Bless run is in progress and must reproduce single-flight-20261014-073517 row for row (except the reverted brzozowski negative), which also restores the tree outputs. Lesson recorded: one suite at a time across all caches; R4 reruns from a copied tmp tree.")
inl note_of_harness_agree_fail_6 () = Note ("HARNESS-AGREE-FAIL", 6u32, "2026-10-14T21:22Z", "main-thread", "17:22 done: h1 (agree-fail only when both exits are failure-class), h2, h3, h4 and the runbook companions are applied to test.ps1/harness.psd1. Reviewed run single-flight-20261014-073517 (DISAGREE 0; lua_while_union_pair Wasm now agrees; abi_external_buffer_length_negative C runs, exit 3). Clean rebless single-flight-20261014-095423 reproduces it row for row apart from the restored brzozowski negative. Kept through two installs since (140125, 164608: 0 differences from their reviews). Uncommitted, on the user's commit list.")
