inl wgsl_parallel_lanes () = Task ("WGSL-PARALLEL-LANES", "2026-10-14 07:35 WGSL programs run as one GPU thread (codegen @workgroup_size(1), wgsl-run dispatch_workgroups(1,1,1)), so the GPU gives bit-exact results but no throughput; apps/tibia gpu_sim.spi proves the multi-creature simulator is bit-exact on WGSL (10 ticks, a 3000-tick troll hunt, 20 arena-spot cyclops clears) but one thread took ~74 s vs ~23 s on C (both incl. compile); design: (1) a lane primitive (e.g. !!!!GpuLane() returning global_invocation_id.x, or main taking a u32 lane) and @workgroup_size(64); (2) wgsl-run dispatches ceil(lanes/64) workgroups from SPIRAL_WGSL_LANES, with one i32 result slot per lane and an aggregate (sum, or all-zero for tests); (3) the shared spiral_heap is partitioned per lane (base = lane * heap_words / lanes) so bump allocation never collides; test: a C-vs-WGSL lane sweep where lane i simulates seed i and the per-lane results match C; serves: GPU training/evaluation of the Tibia simulator to take load off the CPU (CPU is the night-run bottleneck)", Feature, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "wgsl,compiler,gpu,tibia", "current", "current")
inl note_of_wgsl_parallel_lanes_1 () = Note ("WGSL-PARALLEL-LANES", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:22Z", "main-thread", "08:22 pack-1 DLL: acceptance sample tmp/pack/pending-samples/wgsl_parallel_lanes compiles (Wgsl/Fsharp/Rust/C); runner SPIRAL_WGSL_LANES=1 exit 7, =8 lanes 7..56, =130 (3 workgroups) lanes 127..129 = 72/76/82 all correct. Next: corpus check, full Wgsl tier vs oracle, install runner into toolchains, add sample.")
inl note_of_wgsl_parallel_lanes_2 () = Note ("WGSL-PARALLEL-LANES", 2u32, "2026-10-14T17:19Z", "main-thread", "13:19 pack-1d review run single-flight-20261014-123744 (candidate DLL plus the new runner via SPIRAL_WGSL_RUN): all 48 Wgsl rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0. The 33 existing rows changed residual (the new lane-aware entry point and SpiralIo header), and 15 new rows were added by widening the list. Install runbook: job tmp/pack-c/INSTALL.md. Waiting on the lib/Tibia corpus check.")
inl note_of_wgsl_parallel_lanes_3 () = Note ("WGSL-PARALLEL-LANES", 3u32, "2026-10-14T18:24Z", "main-thread", "14:24 installed (pack-1d, oracle reblessed from single-flight-20261014-140125, 0 differences vs the review run): lane-aware WGSL entry point plus spiral-wgsl SPIRAL_WGSL_LANES in toolchains; all Wgsl rows agree with C. Left: an acceptance sample in the harness (draft tmp/pack/pending-samples/wgsl_parallel_lanes) and a multi-lane harness tier.")
inl note_of_wgsl_parallel_lanes_4 () = Note ("WGSL-PARALLEL-LANES", 4u32, "2026-10-14T18:27Z", "main-thread", "14:27 acceptance sample in the tree: samples/wgsl_parallel_lanes (gpu_lane through a BackendSwitch, Wgsl arm reads spiral_lane; value (lane^2+7) mod 251). It is on the Wgsl list (50 rows). Installed toolchain: C exit 7, Wgsl exit 7 with one lane, Rust compiles; earlier runner checks covered 8 and 130 lanes. Its oracle rows arrive with the next bless. A multi-lane harness tier (SPIRAL_WGSL_LANES>1, comparing lane outputs) is the remaining step.")
inl note_of_wgsl_parallel_lanes_5 () = Note ("WGSL-PARALLEL-LANES", 5u32, "2026-10-14T18:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 14:40 Tibia lane measurement on the installed pack-1d: the multi-creature simulator runs one arena-spot cyclops clear per lane, bit-exact with C on lanes 0-63 (and 0-63 of 1024); lane index read as u32. Warm wall time 1 / 64 / 256 / 1024 / 4096 lanes: 4.8 / 4.0 / 4.2 / 5.2 / 5.9 s, so ~4 s fixed per launch and ~0.23 ms per clear marginal vs 1.6 ms per clear on one C core; break-even with one core near 4k clears per launch. 16384 lanes hang (WGSL-LANES-LARGE-DISPATCH-HANG).")
