inl tibia_hunting_ground () = Task ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", "Hunting-ground scenario after the P5 stop rule: respawning camp (2 cyclops + 4 trolls, 60 s respawn) on the real arena map (terrain ArenaHunt), patrol routes and a spawn-sweeping rule; route choice as the new decision", Feature, P2, D5, 90u32, Paused, "", "tibia,simulator,scenario", "current", "current")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:32Z", "user", "2026-10-14 09:32 greedy one-step movement sticks behind walls on the real map (knight frozen at 110,88 chasing a monster at 115,93). terrain.routed_step: bit-parallel BFS over the 61x61 row masks (two u32 words per row, raw Spiral arrays), 4-connected because a diagonal step costs 3 straight ones (Canary A*: 25 vs 10), only on ArenaHunt so every ArenaSpot pin stays bit-exact. Held-out XP over 100 five-minute hunts: standing at the start 87650, hand route 111800, spawn-side loop 115320, spawn sweeper 115270, route evolved on training seeds (16 gens x 8 pairs, a 2-point shuttle at 117,92-116,96) 116220. Leaving the start pays 33%; every route is within 1% of the others because cyclops kill speed, not routing, caps XP. No deaths anywhere. Next lever candidates: an overpopulated ground (more spawns than kill speed) where avoiding being surrounded and kind-aware targeting decide.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-14T13:46Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 09:46 correction of the previous note (route ties): paired over 100 held-out seeds with the cavebot heal tuned on training (Experience objective, heal 110), the evolved shuttle beats the hand route by 4.0% experience (paired t 5.6) at equal profit (t 1.05) and the spawn-side loop and the sweeper by 0.8% (t 1.5-1.6, n.s.); walking vs standing +27.6% (t 21.6). Experience is now an objective GADT case, so it is judged only via judged_on (held-out). Six cyclops (overpopulated): cavebot + sweeper 135300 held-out XP, no deaths; rules evolved under an XP floor return the cavebot (heal 146 + 4, never retreat); retreat-at-2 + sweep trades 6.3% XP for 36.7% lower cost; the evolved shuttle dies twice in training. Monsters on ArenaHunt move 4-connected while ArenaSpot keeps diagonal steps (fidelity note).")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-14T13:51Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 09:51 reproducing central_shuttle_route: route_evolved_on (arena_hunt ()) (spawn_side_loop_route ()) 160 77u32 (training_block ()) 16 8 (search seed 77, start the spawn-side loop, heal 160, 16 generations x 8 antithetic pairs, training seeds 1-100, objective experience minus 5000 per death). The six-cyclops numbers so far are probe results with heal 160 fixed, not pinned and not tuned.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-14T14:09Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 10:09 respawn-time robustness (held-out XP, cavebot heal 110; standing / hand / loop / sweeper / shuttle): 30 s 87980 / 123010 / 126040 / 131810 / 130460; 60 s 87650 / 111800 / 115320 / 115270 / 116220; 120 s 39200 / 79060 / 79980 / 80000 / 80000. The shuttle evolved at 60 s wins only at 60 s; the timer-aware sweeper rule is best or tied at every respawn time. Probe only, not pinned.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 5u32, "2026-10-14T14:12Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 10:12 live hunting ground, staged not applied: canary-monster.xml of data-canary is empty (no natural spawns), so tibia-local/hunting-ground-monster.xml holds the simulator's six spawns at server = simulator + (1833,1250) with spawntime 60; a hunting-ground scenario would swap it in before canary starts and restore the empty file after, leaving the arena clears untouched. Missing for a live run: patrol/sweep logic in live.spi (Lua) and a 5-minute hunt probe. First the router itself gets a live check (BENCHMARK PC-1, probe-path-body.lua, staged).")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 6u32, "2026-10-14T20:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:00 PC-1 live path check: 5 valid runs, the cyclops behind the room wall chases along exactly the router's path (north through the gap, west along the row; 9/9/9/8 steps as predicted) after idling 10-12 s near its spawn; greedy steps would never arrive. New gaps: per-tile ground speed (row 1338 about 455 ms per cyclops step vs about 705 elsewhere) and the ~10 s delay before monsters chase a freshly logged-in knight.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 7u32, "2026-10-14T22:50Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:50 per-tile ground speed on ArenaHunt (terrain.on_ground_at, road masks from appearances.dat bank speeds via otbm-walkability.py --speeds; road 100 vs arena ground 160, the from-tile rule seen in PC-1; model 702/438 ms vs live ~705/455). Re-pinned held-out results: hunting ground (heal tuned 100) standing 89020, hand route 109700, loop 112470, pre-road evolved shuttle 118810, sweeper 119760 (the sweeper now leads); six cyclops (heal tuned 110) standing cavebot 121050 / 0 / -184112, sweeping cavebot -12000 / 30 deaths, shuttle 103600 / 7, retreat standing 100950 / 0 / -107900, retreat + sweep 127200 / 0 / -150159 (leads); duo shared sweep 259350 / -180187 vs territories 248550 / -233638, evolved duo rules 261750 / -180890 (stop rule still holds). Earlier numbers in this item predate roads.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 8u32, "2026-10-14T22:58Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:58 PC-2 (pre-registered road check, not fitted): cyclops chasing along the road steps 452 ms on average (24 steps, 4 valid runs; pre-registered row-1338 subset 456 ms), model 438 ms, uniform ground 702: the per-tile ground speed holds out of sample.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 9u32, "2026-10-14T23:03Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 19:03 route re-evolved with roads (seed 77, start spawn-side loop, heal 160, 16 x 8 on training seeds): a two-point shuttle 121,86 - 117,102, held-out 118720 XP vs the sweeper 119760; the timer-aware rule still beats the evolved route.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 10u32, "2026-10-14T23:12Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 19:12 corrections to note 7: (1) the six-cyclops sweeping cavebot had reused the standing cavebot's tuned heal (110) and died 30 times; with its own heal tuned on training (shaped_cavebot_heal_tuned_on, 190) it earns 138900 / 0 deaths / -254055, the most XP, and retreat + sweep (127200 / -150159) trades 8% XP for 41% lower cost (pinned). (2) Respawn robustness with roads (heal 100): 30 s standing 117190, hand 133170, loop 126330, sweeper 126980, shuttle 133200; 60 s as pinned; 120 s 44510 / 69880 / 80000 / 80000 / 80000: the sweeper is not robust across respawn times any more, fixed routes win at 30 s.")
inl note_of_tibia_hunting_ground_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND", 11u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: the remaining 10% is a live check: no live probe has walked the hunting-ground route yet (PC-1/PC-2 checked single chases only). Next: pre-register one sweeper run against the simulator's clear time.")
inl tibia_party () = Task ("TIBIA-PARTY", "Several characters on the hunting ground (the next scenario design after TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND)", Feature, P3, D5, 40u32, Paused, "", "tibia,simulator,scenario", "current", "current")
inl note_of_tibia_party_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARTY", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:59Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 09:59 written before any code. Order: (1) a hunter record and a party band of size 1, accepted only when every existing pin is unchanged, gpu_sim's WGSL twin included; (2) then a second knight. Decision rules are not expected to express well: splitting the six-cyclops ground into territories vs moving together (one tanks while the other kills, pulls staggered so no knight faces more than two). Hand rules to beat: both sweep the nearest spawn and avoid each other's target; both follow one leader. Stop rule: if the best hand rule lands within 5% of the best evolved party tactic on held-out experience at equal or lower cost, stop; the party lever is then saturated too. Not before P4 has nExBot and the random control live (PR-3).")
inl note_of_tibia_party_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARTY", 2u32, "2026-10-14T14:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 10:40 step 1 done: hunting_pack.hunter record nested in pack (world state stays in pack; knight changes through with_hunter/hunter_steps); pack_sim 23/23 and gpu_sim 6/6 unchanged, so every pin is bit-exact including the WGSL twins. Step 2 (second knight) waits per the note above.")
inl note_of_tibia_party_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARTY", 3u32, "2026-10-14T15:02Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 11:02 step 2 (probe, C only; Kino gate pending because a suite next to the live PR-4 block got both reaped): pack gains ally : hunter, camp.party (1 or 2); the second knight acts through turned (swap ally and hunter, run the unchanged code, swap back), monsters chase and strike the nearer knight the same way, call_sign offsets its RNG entities by 100; solo hunts unchanged (seed 1001 still 18 / 1140 / 20). Six cyclops, 100 held-out hunts, party XP (death -5000) / deaths / profit: solo cavebot sweep 135300 / 0 / -241191; duo cavebot standing 191400 / 0 / -98649; duo cavebot shared sweep 236350 / 1 / -172914; duo territories (border 119) 234750 / 0 / -228350, (115) 232350 / 0 / -221823; duo retreat standing 156450 / 0 / -91826; duo retreat shared sweep 232350 / 0 / -177360; duo retreat territories 229650 / 0 / -207419. Splitting the ground costs ~30% more for no XP: alone, each knight faces the cyclops; moving together (both on the same rule) is the strong hand rule. Next: evolve the duo rules for the stop rule (search waits for memory).")
inl note_of_tibia_party_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARTY", 4u32, "2026-10-14T15:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 11:13 stop rule reached: rules evolved for the duo on training seeds (search seed 91, 12 gens x 12 offspring, objective profit at the shared-sweep cavebot's training XP 237100) return heal 117 + 6 per attacker, never retreat: held-out 238300 XP / 1 death / -170319 vs the shared-sweep cavebot 236350 / 1 / -172914, +0.8% XP and +1.5% profit, inside the 5% bar. The party lever is saturated; the code (ally, turned, call_sign, SweepsTerritory) stays as scenario capability. Kino gate for the ally change still pending (run when the live box is idle).")
inl note_of_tibia_party_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARTY", 5u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: unchanged state (duo views, ally via swap, shared-rule result); stays paused behind POTION-FIDELITY because two-knight live runs need the potion model first.")
inl eoie_note_author () = Task ("EOIE-NOTE-AUTHOR", "agile note records author=user unless --as is passed, so an agent's note is attributed to the user (found 2026-10-14 10:06 by the Tibia lane: TIBIA-HUNTING-GROUND note 1). Default the author from the session (an env var such as EOIE_AUTHOR) or require --as", TaskKind, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "eoie,agile,friction", "current", "current")
inl note_of_eoie_note_author_1 () = Note ("EOIE-NOTE-AUTHOR", 1u32, "2026-10-15T10:47Z", "main-thread", "06:47 groom: still reproduces on eoie.exe of 10-15: agile note without --as records author=user (scratch root tmp/groom-root, T-ONE). Every agent writer passes --as today, so the risk is a forgotten flag silently attributing agent text to the user. Fix direction: require --as, or default to the lease holder. Raised P3 -> P2 because it corrupts provenance, which agent-sync relies on.")
inl note_of_eoie_note_author_2 () = Note ("EOIE-NOTE-AUTHOR", 2u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: agile note refuses an unnamed agent author: EOIE_AUTHOR first, else exit 2 when AI_AGENT or CLAUDECODE is set, else user (agile_task_notes, rust_std_env variable_or_empty); built, deployed, strict renewal passed. Uncommitted; the user commits.")
inl spiral_macro_arg_expressions () = Task ("SPIRAL-MACRO-ARG-EXPRESSIONS", "Found 2026-10-14 10:13 by the Tibia lane (apps/tibia/terrain.spi route_between): a !!!! macro argument cannot be an application, an operator expression over one, or another macro; !!!!ArrayIndexSet(rows, row, arena_spot_low row ^^^ all_bits ()) and word_holds !!!!ArrayIndex(open_lows, row) bit are parse errors (Expected: ) / the block is left out of its module). Accept full expressions as macro arguments (parenthesized at least), or point the error at the argument with a hint to bind it first", TaskKind, P3, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "spiral,parser,macros", "current", "current")
inl note_of_spiral_macro_arg_expressions_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-MACRO-ARG-EXPRESSIONS", 1u32, "2026-10-14T14:58Z", "main-thread", "10:58 narrowed on the installed DLL (job tmp/rotation/macroargs). These compile: an application argument !!!!ArrayIndexSet(xs, 0i32, f 3i32); a macro inside an application f !!!!ArrayIndex(xs, 0i32); a parenthesized operator expression (f 1i32 +. f 2i32). Only a BARE operator expression fails (f 1i32 +. f 2i32, or arena_spot_low row ^^^ all_bits ()), as an unspecific 'block fails to parse'. Cause: the !!!! branch (spiral_compiler.fs ~45176) parses each argument with application, and the operators Pratt parser cannot be reused directly because ',' is its pair operator. Workaround: parenthesize the argument. Fix options: (a) parse arguments with operators at a precedence above ',', or (b) a MacroArgumentNeedsParentheses error at the operator token, the way MalformedTestHeader names its cause.")
inl note_of_spiral_macro_arg_expressions_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-MACRO-ARG-EXPRESSIONS", 2u32, "2026-10-15T01:36Z", "lane-a", "21:36 patch drafted: lane-a/patches/macro-arg-expressions.ps1 parses each !!!! argument with the operators Pratt loop at a floor of ',' precedence (operator_chain, no trailing annotation); repros macro_arg_operator/parenthesized (expect exit 11, same residual); Debug build waits for the heavy gate")
inl note_of_spiral_macro_arg_expressions_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-MACRO-ARG-EXPRESSIONS", 3u32, "2026-10-15T02:18Z", "lane-a", "22:18 verified on Debug -CoreSource (tree + pack-1f patches + this): bare operator args compile to the parenthesized residual CAF029746E56 (run exit 11); !!!!Global with a bare ^^ chain = joined literal residual 9FA5DD1AE125; verify-patches 20/20. Sent to main for the next pack (needs main's corpus check)")
inl note_of_spiral_macro_arg_expressions_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-MACRO-ARG-EXPRESSIONS", 4u32, "2026-10-15T06:15Z", "main-thread", "02:15 installed in pack-1g: '!!!!' macro arguments parse as operator expressions binding tighter than the tuple comma. Review = pack-1f oracle on every cell (no residual change), bless single-flight-20261015-015332, corpus check passed.")
inl note_of_spiral_macro_arg_expressions_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-MACRO-ARG-EXPRESSIONS", 5u32, "2026-10-15T08:15Z", "lane-a", "04:15 installed in pack-1g (main); formatter now emits bare operator macro arguments for split strings and they compile to the joined residuals on 1g (5 eoie packages)")
inl wgsl_tail_call_in_match () = Task ("WGSL-TAIL-CALL-IN-MATCH", "Found 2026-10-14 10:18 by the Tibia lane: on WGSL a let rec whose tail call sits inside a match arm (match c with | NoRoute => if .. elif cond then layers (k + 1) else .. | _ => c) is emitted as a recursive function, and naga rejects it (declaration of sp_layers_9 is recursive); moving the tail call into a plain if/else makes it a loop and the twin is bit-exact (apps/tibia/terrain.spi route_between, gpu_sim.spi a_hunting_ground_hunt_with_routing_on_gpu). Lower tail calls in match arms to loops too, or report it at compile time", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "wgsl,compiler,tibia", "current", "current")
inl note_of_wgsl_tail_call_in_match_1 () = Note ("WGSL-TAIL-CALL-IN-MATCH", 1u32, "2026-10-14T14:56Z", "main-thread", "10:56 cause: codegenWgsl's self_tail had no TyUnionUnbox case (Rust/Delphi/Zig have it), so a let rec whose tail call sits in a match arm was not lowered to a loop and stayed recursive. Fixed in source: the case is added. Union arms already receive the tail context and are emitted as if/else chains, so the continue is legal WGSL. Regression sample samples/wgsl_tail_call_in_match: C exits 10; the installed DLL's WGSL fails naga validation. It lands with pack-1c.")
inl note_of_wgsl_tail_call_in_match_2 () = Note ("WGSL-TAIL-CALL-IN-MATCH", 2u32, "2026-10-14T18:24Z", "main-thread", "14:24 installed with pack-1d; samples/wgsl_tail_call_in_match is on the Wgsl list and agrees with C (exit 10) in single-flight-20261014-140125.")
inl wgsl_lanes_large_dispatch_hang () = Task ("WGSL-LANES-LARGE-DISPATCH-HANG", "Found 2026-10-14 14:40 by the Tibia lane: spiral-wgsl with SPIRAL_WGSL_LANES=16384 on a 2 MB simulator shader (one arena clear per lane) hangs over 10 minutes with no output (4096 lanes finish in 5.9 s, so ~9 s was expected); likely one dispatch outliving the Windows GPU timeout (TDR) and the runner waiting on a lost device. Chunk dispatches under the TDR budget and report device loss as an error. Repro: C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\ac4b4e98\\tmp\\typecheck\\lanes.spi --backend Wgsl", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "wgsl,runner,gpu,tibia", "current", "current")
inl note_of_wgsl_lanes_large_dispatch_hang_1 () = Note ("WGSL-LANES-LARGE-DISPATCH-HANG", 1u32, "2026-10-14T18:43Z", "main-thread", "14:43 main: fix written. Codegen: SpiralIo's pad word becomes lane_base, the lane is lane_base + invocation.x, and the heap slot is per chunk invocation. Runner (tests/native-shims/wgsl-run): SPIRAL_WGSL_CHUNK lanes per submission (default 1024); each chunk rewrites only the header words after code; every wait is a bounded poll with a device-lost callback, exiting 1 with 'device lost ... lower SPIRAL_WGSL_CHUNK' or a timeout (SPIRAL_WGSL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, default 120). Proven with a hand-patched shader: 20000 lanes in 20 chunks in 4 s, all 20000 lane values correct, lane 0's exit code kept. Old one-lane shaders run unchanged on the new runner (5/5 = C). The device-lost path is untested (TDR cannot be forced here). Ships as pack-1e.")
inl note_of_wgsl_lanes_large_dispatch_hang_2 () = Note ("WGSL-LANES-LARGE-DISPATCH-HANG", 2u32, "2026-10-14T19:56Z", "main-thread", "15:56 pack-1e review single-flight-20261014-150624: all 49 Wgsl rows changed residual (lane_base) and still agree with C; 0 behaviour changes against the installed oracle; DISAGREE 0. Install after lane B's corpus check (tmp/pack-c/INSTALL-1e.md).")
inl note_of_wgsl_lanes_large_dispatch_hang_3 () = Note ("WGSL-LANES-LARGE-DISPATCH-HANG", 3u32, "2026-10-14T21:08Z", "main-thread", "17:08 installed with pack-1e: the oracle was reblessed from single-flight-20261014-164608, which reproduces review 150624 on all 4143 rows; the chunking spiral-wgsl is in toolchains. Tibia notified.")
inl note_of_wgsl_lanes_large_dispatch_hang_4 () = Note ("WGSL-LANES-LARGE-DISPATCH-HANG", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:49Z", "main-thread", "06:49 groom: chunked dispatch installed since pack-1e; Wgsl 50/50 agree in the pack-1h oracle and no hang in 8 full suites tonight. Done.")
inl tibia_potion_fidelity () = Task ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", "Potion use is the open fidelity gap (PR-4, 2026-10-14 14:53): the simulator predicts 13.23 potions per cyclops clear for the rules policy and 9.09 for the retreat policy, live is 11.53 and 12.90 (clear times match within noise). Candidates to measure: live potion cooldown and exhaust vs the model, heal amount distribution, how often a live retreat step costs an attack turn or draws extra hits (retreat damage 2217 vs rules 2029 live), block-charge regain while moving. Fix the model, then re-run the prediction check before designing more policies in the simulator", Story, P0, D5, 80u32, Paused, "", "tibia,fidelity,simulator", "current", "current")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-10-14T18:59Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 14:59 first diagnosis (PR-4 logs vs 100 simulated held-out clears): damage per landed hit matches (live 34.1-34.5, model 34.97), so the gap is the number of hits. Rules: simulator 65.1 hits / 2266 damage per clear vs live 59.0 / 2012 (about 10% too many). Retreat: simulator 45.9 / 1617 vs live 64.0 / 2207: the simulator's retreat avoids 30% of the hits, live retreat takes 8% more than rules. Live retreat steps 9.1 times per clear but is cornered on 421 decision ticks per clear (every retreat tile taken or blocked); the simulated knight steps 4.9 times and is never cornered. Live cyclops surround the knight; the simulator's do not, so its escape route does not exist live. Next: log live monster positions per tick around the knight (a probe like probe-path-body) and compare the occupancy pattern with the simulator's; suspects are monster step choice when the direct tile is taken (Canary picks among equal-cost tiles, the model's best_step order is fixed) and the diagonal rule.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 2u32, "2026-10-14T19:46Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 15:46 PR-2 (mixed camp, 20 live runs, clean harness) shows the same pattern: clear time holds (37.3 vs 36.2 s, t 0.62), potions overpredicted (live 0.55 vs 1.23 per clear, t -3.43).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 3u32, "2026-10-14T20:44Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:44 standing-policy gap explained: live the knight takes 1.8 hits in the first 10 s of a rules clear, the simulator 7.9; PC-1 independently measured monsters idling ~10 s after the knight logs in. camp.wakes_at (default 0, existing pins unchanged) with live_wake_ms () = 10000 (from PC-1, not fitted to PR-4): rules 11.44 potions / 90.1 s / 56.9 hits (live 11.53 / 87.6 / 59.0), mixed 0.42 / 37.7 s (live 0.55 / 37.3), both within noise; pinned in pack_sim (with_the_live_wake_delay_the_standing_clears_match_the_live_arena). Remaining: retreat 7.26 predicted vs 12.90 live (escape modeling: live knight cornered against walls), random control 106.8 / 138.5 s vs 94.1 / 102.7 (live auto-attack persists between random picks). Out-of-sample live check of the wake model: PR-6.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 4u32, "2026-10-14T22:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:00 PR-6 (out-of-sample, 2 cyclops, 20 live runs, clean): clear time holds (62.5 vs 59.3 s), potions fail for both models (live 4.85 vs wake 8.25, t -12.0; no wake 10.14). Live hits per clear 30.7 vs simulated 43.4 at the same damage per hit: the per-cyclops landed-hit rate is too high in the simulator; the 3-cyclops match (PR-4) was partly offsetting errors. Next: measure the live landed-hit rate per adjacent cyclops-second (log monster adjacency per tick) and Canary's attack interval/chance and target switching for cyclops.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 5u32, "2026-10-14T22:11Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:11 exploratory adjacency diagnostic (tibia-local/probe-policy-diag-body.lua, 3 live 2-cyclops rules clears, tibia-local/adjacency-diagnostic.txt; not pre-registered): live 84.9 / 113.6 / 78.1 adjacent cyclops-seconds per clear and 0.342 / 0.378 / 0.358 landed hits per adjacent cyclops-second. Simulator (wake 10 s, 100 held-out clears): 105.9 adjacent cyclops-seconds per clear and 0.409 landed hits per adjacent cyclops-second. Both factors are about 15% high (product 1.31 of the 1.41 hit gap). Suspects: Canary runs monster attacks on its 1 s creature-think tick (a fresh adjacency waits for the next think), and the second cyclops reaches the knight later live. Verify against Canary's monster.cpp onThink/doAttacking before changing the model.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 6u32, "2026-10-14T22:11Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:11 source check (opentibiabr/canary main, src/creatures/monsters/monster.cpp, read-only; our server is 3.6.1, so verify against that tag): the wake delay is login protection: target selection and attacks return false while player->isLoginProtected(). Melee cadence: attackTicks advance on creature-think intervals and fire when attackTicks % speed >= interval, plus a 1500 ms melee gate since lastMeleeAttack; a fresh adjacency waits for the next think. Next session: read the 3.6.1 tag's monster.cpp/player.cpp (login protection duration, think interval), model attacks on think ticks, then re-run PR-6's prediction as a new pre-registration.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 7u32, "2026-10-14T22:31Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:31 3.6.1 facts: loginProtectionTime = 10 * 1000 (tibia-local/canary/config.lua) confirms the wake; cyclops melee interval 2000 chance 100, staticAttackChance 90 (data-canary cyclops.lua); EVENT_CREATURE_THINK_INTERVAL 1000 in 10 buckets of 100 ms (v3.6.1 creature.hpp); doAttacking adds the think interval to attackTicks, the melee fires when speed <= attackTicks and the target is in range, and attackTicks resets either way (a missed range check loses the swing). Modeled as a think-grid cadence (strike only on a fixed 2 s grid per creature): predictions move under 1% (3 cyclops 11.35 vs 11.44; 2 cyclops 8.17 vs 8.25; rate 0.406 vs 0.409), so cadence is not the cause; change reverted, PR-7 not run. Lead: in the simulator the landed rate per adjacent cyclops rises with attackers (1 cyclops 0.361, 2-3 cyclops 0.41) because two block charges absorb more of one attacker's hits; live two cyclops land 0.36, the simulator's one-cyclops rate. Next: check Canary 3.6.1 blockHit / blockCount regain and the knight's shield/armor reduction live (count blocked attacks per clear).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 8u32, "2026-10-14T22:32Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:32 v3.6.1 creature.cpp: blockCount +1 per 1000 ms of think, cap 2, consumed whenever defense or armor is checked (as modeled); armor applies without charges; afterwards mitigateDamage reduces nonzero damage and can zero it (BLOCK_ARMOR) - not modeled. Sharpest summary of the gap: with one swing per 2 s while adjacent, live two-cyclops clears land about 67% of swings (30.7 landed of about 46 opportunities per clear), the simulator about 82% (43.4 of about 53). Next session: model Canary's player mitigation (mitigateDamage, 3.6.1 formula) and recheck damage per landed hit (currently calibrated to live 34) and landed fraction together; then pre-register a fresh live check.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 9u32, "2026-10-14T22:33Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 18:33 mitigateDamage (v3.6.1): damage = trunc(damage - damage * mitigation / 100.0), zeroed only when that reaches 0, i.e. 1-damage hits at mitigation below 50%; it cannot remove 15 points of landed swings, so it is not the lead. Remaining candidate: the defense path (Player canUseDefense conditions and the shield roll damage -= uniform(defense/2, defense) while a charge is available) against combat.spi's calibrated block; measure live blocked swings directly (block magic effects on the knight's tile) before modeling.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 10u32, "2026-10-14T23:22Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 19:22 random control (explanatory, PR-5 motivated): added live auto-attack (once in reach the knight keeps swinging whatever the random pick); with the 10 s wake the 200 s-capped arena prediction becomes 103.4 s per clear (live 102.7) and 81.1 potions per run (live 94.1): time fixed, potions now under. Drink rate simulator 0.78/s vs live 0.92/s at 25% drink picks per 100 ms: the live potion exhaust or its interaction with the client's attempts differs from vocations.knight_heal's cooldown; measure the live gap between consecutive potions.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 11u32, "2026-10-14T23:29Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 19:29 potion gate (exploratory, tibia-local/potion-gap-diagnostic.txt, 2 live random-control clears): the client attempted 138 and 146 drinks, the server accepted 99 and 94 (72%), about 0.92 accepted per second; attempt gaps bottom out at 300 ms (parity gate plus the decision tick). Canary data/scripts/actions/items/potions.lua sets the heal exhaust to timeBetweenExActions - 1000 = 0 ms (config.lua timeBetweenExActions = 1000, timeBetweenActions = 200), so potions are gated by the ex-action delay, not a 1 s heal cooldown; the accepted rate suggests an effective gate near 0.7 s. The simulator's random control drinks 0.78/s. Next: log accepted-potion times server-side (or from the client's text-message arrival) and replace vocations.knight_heal's cooldown with the measured gate; this also affects every policy's potion timing near the threshold.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 12u32, "2026-10-14T23:42Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 19:42 correction of note 11: accepted-potion times (server 'Using one of' text arrival, tibia-local/potion-accept-diagnostic.txt, 2 live random-control clears, 155 potions) are 959 / 997 / 1006 / 1011 ms (min, p10, p25, median), mean 1100: the gate is 1000 ms, as the model's cooldown says, not ~0.7 s. The rate difference comes from queuing: an attempt made during the exhaust is held and executed when it ends (gaps cluster at 1000-1011 ms), while the simulated random control only attempts after the cooldown and then waits for its next 25% pick (~1.3 s gaps). Model fix for later: a drink requested during the cooldown runs at the cooldown's end (also relevant to live policies whose client timer fires a little early).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 13u32, "2026-10-15T04:15Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 00:15 diagnosis and fix: (1) simulator bug: start created slots 0-2 alive regardless of camp size, so 1- and 2-cyclops camps fielded 3 cyclops (PR-6's prediction modeled the wrong scenario); fixed (placed for every slot), size-3/6 pins unchanged. (2) live landed-damage shape (6446 hits) fits a defense of ~17-18 vs the modeled 15, so blocking is close; live swing gaps cluster at ~2.2 s (37 gaps, one scenario; kept on record, not adopted). (3) the main gap was surrounding: live cyclops get ~1.75 adjacent with two monsters, the simulator ~1, because greedy steps (and the 4-connected BFS) cannot detour around another creature; added terrain.weighted_step (Canary-style weights 10/25, creatures as obstacles, chamfer sweeps over a window) for the arena spot; ArenaHunt keeps the BFS (pins unchanged there; weighted is 17x slower on long distances). Re-pinned: 6 pack_sim tests (3 renamed where the claim changed: arena clear takes the live time; evolved rules save potions at a slightly slower clear; mixed-camp evolved rules now dominate the tuned cavebot), gpu_sim twin now 5 clears (bit-exact on WGSL). PR-7 (pre-registered, 2 cyclops, retreat policy, 20 live runs): predicted 4.67 potions, live 5.45, t 1.95: holds; greedy alternative 3.49 fails (t 4.89).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 14u32, "2026-10-15T04:23Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 00:23 no live policy candidate yet: rules evolved under the validated model (login protection + occupancy-aware router; CheapClearWithin cavebot time +15%, seed 31, 8 x 8) choose heal below 101 + 10 per attacker, retreat at 1: held-out 11.24 potions / 1 death / 100.2 s vs rules heal 160 13.34 / 0 / 88.4 s, a time-for-potions trade with a death, not a win. The model still ranks rules vs retreat against live (simulated rules 13.3 > retreat 12.0; live rules 11.5 < retreat 12.9), so policy design waits for the remaining gap (rules overpredicted by ~1.8 potions).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 15u32, "2026-10-15T10:05Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 06:10: model vs pooled live, 100 held-out clears (router + size fix + wake): 2 cyc rules 5.16 vs 4.85 (PR-6), retreat 4.62 vs 5.45 (PR-7); 3 cyc rules 13.34 vs 12.22 (PR-4+PR-8, n60), retreat 11.78 vs 12.62 (PR-4+PR-3a, n50). The retreat deficit is the same at both sizes (-0.83/-0.84): a per-retreat cost is missing. Lead (Canary source): classicAttackSpeed=false schedules the next swing as nextActionTask and Player::onWalk clears it, so after any knight step the swing resumes on the next 1 s think (or hasExtraSwing on a creature move). Scratch variant (hunter_steps sets attack_ready_at = strike_ready_at = ceil1000(max(now, strike ready))): retreat 3 cyc 12.14 potions / 90.6 s (live 12.62 / ~91.1), 2 cyc 4.72; rules unchanged. Explains ~40%/12% of the gap. Next: adopt it (re-pin pack_sim + GPU twins), pre-register an out-of-sample check, then look for the rest (retreat re-engage path: probe DontChase/chase toggling, knight step speed during retreats).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 16u32, "2026-10-15T10:06Z", "tibia-lane", "Hit counts match live: rules PR-8 64.07 hits taken per clear (model 64.17), retreat PR-3a 59.05 (model ~58.4); live damage per landed hit retreat 35.73 vs rules 34.5 (about 1.3 se apart, block path in Creature::blockHit matches the model, so treat as noise for now). Live retreat per clear: 12 retreat steps, 324 cornered ticks (no free tile). The residual potion gap is small (retreat 3 cyc t ~1.7 on n50; PR-8 rules alone 12.9 vs 13.34) - next session: adopt step-cancels-swing, then pre-register.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 17u32, "2026-10-15T10:16Z", "tibia-lane", "06:15: adopted as an opt-in camp rule: hunting_pack union swing_after_step (SwingKeepsItsTime default | SwingWaitsForThink), swinging_on_think, swing_after_step applied in hunter_steps; pinned by pack_sim test after_a_step_the_swing_waits_for_the_next_think_so_retreating_costs_more_potions_and_rules_stay (retreat 1178->1214 potions/100, hits 5747->5856; rules 1336). 69/69 tests pass memo off. Next: pre-register an out-of-sample live check of the swing rule (e.g. retreat at 1 cyclops or retreat at 1 attacker), then make it the live-mirroring default.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_18 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 18u32, "2026-10-15T10:17Z", "tibia-lane", "06:18: clear-level checks cannot validate the swing rule: predictions keep vs think, 100 held-out clears: 3 cyc retreat-at-1 11.58 vs 11.62 potions, 94.1 vs 95.9 s (sd ~11 s; knight mostly cornered); 1 cyc retreat-at-1 0.60 vs 0.68, 33.6 vs 33.7 s; the 3 cyc retreat-at-2 effect (+0.36) needs ~1500 runs. Validate the mechanic directly instead (PC-3, to pre-register): timestamp server texts and knight steps in probe-policy-body.lua; prediction: gaps between consecutive landed knight hits are multiples of 2000 ms when no knight step falls between them, and 2000k + 0..1000 ms when one does (swing resumes on the 1 s think).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_19 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 19u32, "2026-10-15T10:20Z", "tibia-lane", "Correction: the note stamped '2026-10-15 06:10' was written at 06:05 (clock read after writing).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_20 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 20u32, "2026-10-15T10:38Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 06:37: PC-3 (pre-registered 06:24, BENCHMARK) HOLDS: 5 live retreat runs, landed knight hits timestamped; pairs without a step 101/106 on the 2000 ms grid, pairs spanning a knight step 31/36 late by 60-1060 ms (2 on grid). Delays cluster at 150-200 ms (median ~180): the swing mostly resumes on hasExtraSwing when a following cyclops moves (Creature::onCreatureMove), sooner than the next think; the model's swinging_on_think (phase-0 think, ~500 ms mean) is the right direction and probably too long. Next: model the resume as min(next think, next adjacent-creature move once overdue), re-check potions. Tools: probe-policy-body.lua @t+ stamps, pc3-analysis.ps1 (call in-process with -Logs array).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_21 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 21u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: stays P0 and first on the roadmap: next is modeling the shorter live swing delay (PC-3) and re-checking potions.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_22 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 22u32, "2026-10-15T12:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 08:14 root cause found and modeled. Potions per 1000 hp of damage are the same live and simulated (~5.8), so the gap was hits. The old simulator replayed ONE geometry for every seed (fixed spawn, monsters frozen during the 10 s wake, deterministic paths); live, cyclopes idle-wander during login protection (Canary Monster::doRandomStep: a random free cardinal step once 1000 ms passed since the last move), so every clear differs and the retreat knight ends cornered in the pocket at 1936,1349 (43% of live samples). Also measured: the live cyclops swing period is 2166 ms (28/30 single-cyclops landed gaps; Canary's 100 ms creature check runs ~8 ms late per cycle). New opt-in camp rules: wandering_while_idle (idle_behavior), meleeing_every (live_creature_strike_ms 2166, cadence kept across 100 ms ticks), knight_standing_at (knight_placement), swing rule generalized to SwingWaitsForThinkOrMove (swinging_like_canary), footing StepAwayLikeTheLiveProbe (exact probe candidates); bundled as mirroring_the_live_arena + live_retreat_tactic. Model vs live (explanatory, in-sample): 3 cyc rules 12.74 vs 12.22 (t~-1.2), retreat 11.77 vs 12.62 (t~1.7); 2 cyc rules 4.83 vs 4.85, retreat 5.09 vs 5.45; clear times all within 2 s; rules hits 61.3 vs 61.5. 3-cyc ranking still off by ~1.4 (borderline). Pinned by pack_sim test mirroring_the_live_arena_predicts_rules_and_retreat_within_the_live_noise_at_two_and_three_cyclops. Ruled out on the way: Canary think-based monster melee with a 1000 ms think (widens the retreat gap; removed), probe-exact escape candidates alone (no effect on the old fixed geometry). Policy search under the corrected model: heal threshold 160->130 saves 0.28 potions, deaths from 120; the best standing tile (1929,1353) saves 0.32 held-out (winner's curse from 13.0 training). No live-runnable candidate beats rules-160 detectably; PR-9 (rules vs vBot, 50+50) pre-registered instead.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_23 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 23u32, "2026-10-15T18:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 14:14 PR-10 (pre-registered 12:57, out of sample): spiral-reach (rules 160, ReachFirst, never retreats) live 12.30 potions vs predicted 13.51, t -2.43: FAILS; clear time holds (89.1 vs 91.1). The no-targeting-effect alternative (12.74) fits. Live our three policies take the same damage (2110-2149) and potions (12.2-12.5); the model spreads them 11.8-13.5, so it is too sensitive to targeting and retreat. Next: find what makes live exposure policy-insensitive (sim retreat cuts hits 7%, live 5% but with harder hits; sim reach adds 4% hits, live -3%).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_24 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 24u32, "2026-10-15T22:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:40 no-protection side prediction (recorded 15:16 before analysis): rules 15.63 potions, 72.4 hits; live PR-11 rules 14.42, 69.1 hits (about 1.2 potions high, t ~-2.6). Without the wake, the model over-counts hits by ~5%. Open items: policy sensitivity too strong (PR-10), crowding under-counted with protection (34 s vs 32-54 s), hits over-counted without it.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_25 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 25u32, "2026-10-15T22:43Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:43 lead for the PR-10 miss: under mirroring_the_live_arena the simulated knight steps 6.5 times per clear with CurrentFirst and 5.0 with ReachFirst, switching targets 3.0 vs 4.4 times, and ReachFirst takes 2.5 more hits (63.8 vs 61.3). Live the same policies engage 4.1 vs 4.7 targets per clear (strike notes), approach once each, and their hits differ within noise (62.0 vs 60.3). So the simulator charges for standing still and switching more than live does; check how a knight step costs adjacent monsters swings in the sim (strike at once on re-adjacency) against Canary's think-based melee with extraMeleeAttack and the 1500 ms rule, now at the measured ~1083 ms think.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_26 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 26u32, "2026-10-15T22:46Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:46 two follow-ups to the PR-10 lead, no repo change: (1) correction: live CurrentFirst does not switch targets mid-fight; its extra strike notes (4.1 per clear) repeat the same cyclops at the same health (the parity gate dropping and re-sending the attack), so live and simulated switching agree (about one per kill). (2) scratch variant melee-think (run-variant.ps1: Canary think-based monster melee at period/2 = 1083 ms with extraMeleeAttack and the 1500 ms rule): current 12.56 (live 12.46), reach 13.19 (12.30), retreat 11.23 (12.20), no-protection current 15.27 (14.42); mixed, not adopted. The policy-sensitivity gap stays open.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_27 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 27u32, "2026-10-15T22:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:54 no-protection over-count traced to the opening: simulated cyclopes land their first hit about 0.2 s into the clear (strikes_at starts at 0), live about 3.4 s after login (0.9 s after the probe starts); in Canary a monster's attackTicks starts at 0 when it acquires a target, so its first melee waits about two thinks. Scratch variant first-strike-delay (no swing before wake + one period): no-protection rules 15.29 potions / 70.8 hits (was 15.63 / 72.4; live 14.42 / 69.1), 3-cyc rules 12.47, reach 13.22 (live 12.30), retreat 11.75, 2-cyc rules 4.65, retreat 4.74 (live 5.45). Partial, not adopted; together with melee-think it is the next modeling step (Canary's acquisition + attackTicks + extraMeleeAttack, think ~1083 ms), with a pre-registered live check after.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_28 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 28u32, "2026-10-15T22:57Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:57 scored the model variants against all six live potion means (t = (model - live)/se; 3-cyc rules PR-9, reach PR-10, retreat PR-3a+PR-4, 2-cyc rules PR-6, retreat PR-7, no-protection rules PR-11): current model sum t^2 16.7 with 2 beyond |2| (reach 2.43, no-protection 2.59); first-strike delay 13.5, none beyond |2|; think-based melee 16.3, retreat -2.78. Recommendation for the next session: adopt the first-strike delay (a monster's first melee waits one swing period after it can target; Canary attackTicks starts at 0) as an opt-in camp rule, re-pin, then pre-register a live check on a NEW configuration (all six live sets are now in-sample).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_29 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 29u32, "2026-10-15T23:19Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 19:19 adopted as an opt-in rule: hunting_pack melee_timing case MeleeEveryOnceTargeted (builder meleeing_every_once_targeted): a cyclops's first swing waits one swing period after it can target (Canary attackTicks starts at 0). Pinned by pack_sim test a_cyclops_first_swing_waits_one_period_after_it_can_target_which_fits_six_live_means_best (six comparisons). Verified 19:12-19:18 memo off: pack_sim 27/27, gpu_sim 6/6, hunt_sim 11/11. Not yet in mirroring_the_live_arena (that would re-pin the mirror test); next session: fold it in and pre-register a live check on a new configuration.")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_30 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 30u32, "2026-10-15T23:20Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 19:20 predictions for the next out-of-sample check (fixed harness: mirroring_the_live_arena |> waking_at 0 |> meleeing_every_once_targeted 2166, 100 held-out): rules heal 160 15.29 potions (live PR-11 14.42, in-sample), heal 130 15.04 (sd 2.70, 2 deaths/100), heal 120 14.87 (5 deaths/100). The model still runs ~0.9 high on the fixed harness, so fix that bias before registering a new check; heal thresholds barely move potions (as on the old harness).")
inl note_of_tibia_potion_fidelity_31 () = Note ("TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY", 31u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 paused (user). Resume order: fold meleeing_every_once_targeted into mirroring_the_live_arena and re-pin; fix the ~0.9-potion over-count on the fixed harness; then the policy-sensitivity gap (PR-10); then pre-register an out-of-sample check on a new configuration.")
inl tibia_nexbot_crash () = Task ("TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH", "nExBot 4.0.4 (19632d4) crashes OTClient Redemption 4.x (Aug 15 2026 build) with 0xC0000374 (heap corruption) about 10 s after login, in all 3 PR-3 check runs (2026-10-14 16:33); otclient.log shows no Lua error, and a [nexbot-load] trace before each loadScript (TIBIA_NEXBOT_TRACE=1 in run-policy-scenario.ps1) printed nothing, so the crash precedes module loading or g_logger is not reachable from the bot environment. Next: trace with the bot's own info()/warn() into its storage folder, bisect _Loader.lua phases (styles, sanitizeStorage, ACL init), try an OTClient debug build for the native stack. PR-3 waits for this", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,baselines,nexbot", "current", "current")
inl note_of_tibia_nexbot_crash_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH", 1u32, "2026-10-15T07:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 03:30 root cause found and shimmed: file tracing from the bot's own Lua (TIBIA_NEXBOT_TRACE=1 in run-policy-scenario.ps1, /nexbot-trace.log) shows the crash on the first dofile issued while another dofile is still executing (utils/path_utils.lua loading constants/floor_items.lua, then core/cavebot.lua loading cavebot/*); not pcall (wrapping it changed nothing), not the file. OTClient Redemption's native dofile does not survive nesting (0xC0000374). Shim (TIBIA_NEXBOT_LUA_DOFILE=1, tibia-local/bot-lua-dofile.lua prepended to the runtime _Loader.lua): a pure-Lua dofile (g_resources.readFileContents + loadstring + setfenv to the caller's environment) - the loader then completes all 161 steps and the client exits normally. Next: nExBot misbehaves under the seeded config (TargetBot never attacks; HealBot drinks ~1/s at full health until empty, then the knight dies): fix the seeding (HealBot and TargetBot formats/state for nExBot 4.0.4).")
inl note_of_tibia_nexbot_crash_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH", 2u32, "2026-10-15T08:22Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 04:02: nExBot runs. Causes: (1) native dofile, and any Lua error raised under nExBot's pcall around a nested load, crash OTClient Redemption 0xC0000374; nExBot's own dofile('nExBot/targetbot/chase_controller.lua') names a missing path. Fix: tibia-local/bot-lua-dofile.lua pure-Lua dofile (missing file returns nothing), now default for -Bot nExBot. (2) bot sandbox executor.lua lacked getmetatable/rawset/rawget/rawequal/next/select/unpack/xpcall; added. (3) Canary Game::playerFollowCreature clears the attack target on any follow packet without telling the client; nExBot's one cancelFollow after attack left it never hitting. probe-nexbot-body.lua makes cancelFollow a no-op when nothing is followed. With all three: clear 86.1 s, 17 potions, no death. Harness weakness: a scenario exception leaves Canary running and run-arena hangs on the inherited pipe. PR-3a (retreat vs nexbot, 20 each) pre-registered in BENCHMARK and running.")
inl note_of_tibia_nexbot_crash_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 05:50: PR-3a done (BENCHMARK): 40 runs, 0 harness failures, 0 deaths. Retreat 12.20 vs nExBot 14.55 potions, diff -2.35 (CI -4.58..-0.12), t -2.14 (crit 2.03): significant, narrow, single test; nExBot's mean is near vBot's. The cancelFollow guard fired once in every nExBot run. Shims stay in tibia-local (dofile shim now default for -Bot nExBot; TIBIA_NEXBOT_LUA_DOFILE=0 turns it off). Left open: report the Canary follow/attack desync and nExBot's chase_controller path upstream (user's call).")
inl note_of_tibia_nexbot_crash_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH", 4u32, "2026-10-15T11:04Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:04 correction: the 'report upstream' line in note 3 is withdrawn (user: no interaction with public projects). The bugs stay as local workarounds, recorded in TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS.")
inl lib_rust_testing_globals () = Task ("LIB-RUST-TESTING-GLOBALS", "lib/spiral/rust/testing.spi run_tests' emits Rust globals on every backend: apps/spiral's F# output starts with 'thread_local! { static SPIRAL_TEST ... }' and '#[test] fn verify_app() ...' (installed pack-1g output, lines 1-2). Its two global calls are not behind a Rust backend switch. Fix: put them behind the Rust arm (like fsharp_global for F#), check apps/spiral F# and Rust outputs, run a suite review if any sample reaches run_tests'", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "spiral,lib,backends", "current", "current")
inl note_of_lib_rust_testing_globals_1 () = Note ("LIB-RUST-TESTING-GLOBALS", 1u32, "2026-10-15T06:54Z", "main-thread", "02:54 found during HOPACSOTA D6 (watching globals in apps/spiral). Not done tonight: a lib change can change sample residuals, so it needs its own review and bless window.")
inl note_of_lib_rust_testing_globals_2 () = Note ("LIB-RUST-TESTING-GLOBALS", 2u32, "2026-10-15T07:05Z", "main-thread", "03:05 fixed in lib/spiral/rust/testing.spi: run_tests' guards both global calls with 'if is_rust () then' (a static bool from a full backend switch, so no residual). A partial backend_switch with only a Rust key was tried first and dropped: on F# it leaves a dead string let for the backend name plus two record_type_try_find comment lines. Proof with the installed pack-1g compiler: apps/spiral Rust output byte-identical, F# output loses exactly the two Rust lines (thread_local!, #[test]) and nothing else. No sample reaches run_tests', so the oracle is unaffected.")
inl package_defaults_per_package () = Task ("PACKAGE-DEFAULTS-PER-PACKAGE", "Package numeric defaults (spiproj default-int/default-float/edition) are honored only by the one-shot CLI (host applyPackageDefaults sets SPIRAL_DEFAULT_* before startup). The batch harness, --server-tcp (Kino) and the language server compile with the process-wide default_env (core 7281, 44800 literal parse, 51814/54140 Infer int), so a package declaring default-int: i64 silently gets i32 there. Found by the new regression sample package_default_int_i64 (held in the job tmp until fixed). Fix: thread the package's spiproj defaults into its parse and infer (natural to do with the Infer pair unification).", TaskKind, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "spiral,compiler,packages,bug", "current", "current")
inl note_of_package_defaults_per_package_1 () = Note ("PACKAGE-DEFAULTS-PER-PACKAGE", 1u32, "2026-10-15T12:00Z", "main-thread", "08:00 main: pack-1i review single-flight-20261015-073154 shows the sample failing on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi with Cannot parse the literal as: i32, while the CLI compiles it to int64_t. Sample held at the job's tmp/pack-i/held-samples to avoid blessing wrong behaviour; it comes back with the fix.")
inl note_of_package_defaults_per_package_2 () = Note ("PACKAGE-DEFAULTS-PER-PACKAGE", 2u32, "2026-10-15T13:06Z", "main-thread", "09:06 design (main): the core already threads default_env as a parameter. (1) Inference: derive a per-package DefaultEnv from Schema.defaultInt/defaultFloat/edition (SchemaState.schema, RString options) where each package's state is created and updated (wdiff_projenvr_sync_schema -> wdiff_proj_init; projenv_update_packages -> wdiff_projenv). Re-apply the package's own base types (int/uint/float) after folding dependency envs, because funs.union lets a dependency's base types override the package's. (2) Parsing: unsuffixed literals and edition-3 syntax are read in parse_block via wdiff_module_* at the module-load sites, which need the file's package schema. Planned as pack-1k on top of the Infer unification; the held sample package_default_int_i64 is the regression test.")
inl note_of_package_defaults_per_package_3 () = Note ("PACKAGE-DEFAULTS-PER-PACKAGE", 3u32, "2026-10-15T14:27Z", "main-thread", "10:27 fixed in pack-1k (tmp/pack-k/per_package_defaults.ps1 + host_package_defaults_validate_only.ps1): Schema now carries the spiproj defaults; each package's state is created/updated with its own DefaultEnv; parse uses the file's owning package; a package's own int/uint/float win over dependency base types (union order); the host only validates. Proof so far: the held sample compiles to int64_t through --batch (the path that failed). Review + corpus pending.")
inl note_of_package_defaults_per_package_4 () = Note ("PACKAGE-DEFAULTS-PER-PACKAGE", 4u32, "2026-10-15T15:16Z", "main-thread", "11:16 verified by the suite: pack-1k review single-flight-20261015-105101 compiles package_default_int_i64 on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi through the harness's batch path, C exit 7 and Rust/Delphi agree. No other row changed behaviour. Install after the 12:45 corpus check.")
inl note_of_package_defaults_per_package_5 () = Note ("PACKAGE-DEFAULTS-PER-PACKAGE", 5u32, "2026-10-15T18:26Z", "main-thread", "14:26 installed in pack-1k and blessed (single-flight-20261015-140535); package_default_int_i64 is now a suite row (exit 7 on C/Rust/Delphi). Done.")
inl kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64 () = Task ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", "Kino test cells render wide i64 values as f64 (found 19:10 2026-10-15 by lane B's Lua wide-integer Kino probe): a 9007199254740993i64 literal inside a test cell printed 9007199254740992.0 on Rust too, so the loss is in Kino's test-cell result path (value transport or rendering), not in a backend; plain cells and the harness are exact (Lua suite DISAGREE 0, 64k randomized ops 0 mismatches). Find where the cell value goes through a float and keep integers exact.", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,correctness", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64 () = Planning ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", Unestimated, LoadUnset, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64_1 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", 1u32, "2026-10-15T23:17Z", "lane-b", "lane-b, found by reading the code: the f64 values are not in the program output. They come from Spiral.Kino.shown/1 (apps/kino/lib/spiral/kino.ex, @number regex + same_number/1), which rewrites every number token through Float.parse and float_to_binary(decimals 6, compact) before targets are compared and in the disagreement message. Effects: (1) the message shows 9007199254740993 as 9007199254740992.0; (2) worse, agreement treats integers that differ beyond 2^53 as equal (false agree). Fix patches/kino-test-cell-i64.ps1: integer tokens with abs > 2^53 compare as exact integer text, integral floats beyond 2^53 render as their integer text, everything at or below 2^53 is unchanged; plus a kino_test.exs unit test. Logic checked standalone in elixir; the Kino unit-test run + capture repro wait for the Tibia Kino window. Separate Lua finding from the same probe: console.write line missing in the Kino Lua output (Kino-free the same program prints it), and sm'.format_debug of a record with an i64 field prints the w64 halves on Lua.")
inl note_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64_2 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", 2u32, "2026-10-15T23:19Z", "main-thread", "19:19 main: cause (lane B): Spiral.Kino.shown/1 normalizes every number token through Float.parse + float_to_binary(decimals 6) before the cross-target comparison, so integers beyond 2^53 are both shown wrongly and compared lossily (two targets printing different big integers count as agreeing). Raised P1 -> P0 for the false agreement. Fix staged: lane B patches/kino-test-cell-i64.ps1 (exact integer text beyond 2^53, unchanged at or below), proof run after the Tibia window.")
inl note_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64_3 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", 3u32, "2026-10-15T23:40Z", "lane-b", "19:40 lane-b: kino-test-cell-i64.ps1 applied to the tree (apps/kino/lib/spiral/kino.ex same_number + @f64_exact_integer_limit; test/spiral/kino_test.exs new test). Proof: kino_test.exs number/union/new tests 3/0; Kino Lua-vs-Rust probe message now exact (9007199254740993, 18446744073709551615, -9223372036854775807) instead of 9007199254740992.0. Open: Kino Lua run drops the console.write(a + 1) line (4 lines vs Rust 5) while the same program Kino-free prints 5 lines on Lua 5.1; next step a run-mode capture of the generated main.lua. Lua record format_debug fix staged as patches/lua-format-debug-record.ps1 (needs a Lua harness probe).")
inl note_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64_4 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", 4u32, "2026-10-15T23:40Z", "main-thread", "19:40 main: fixed in the tree (lane B, applied 19:40, reviewed by main): kino.ex same_number keeps integers beyond 2^53 as exact integer text and turns integral floats beyond 2^53 into their integer text; at or below 2^53 unchanged. kino_test.exs new test; 3/3 number tests pass; Lua probe now shows 9007199254740993 / 18446744073709551615 exactly on Rust and Lua. Full mix test on the tree copy pending. Follow-up: Kino's Lua run drops a console.write line (4 vs 5 lines; Kino-free prints 5), needs a run-mode capture.")
inl note_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64_5 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", 5u32, "2026-10-15T23:43Z", "main-thread", "19:43 main: full Kino mix test on the tree copy with this fix + kino-default-zig: 238 tests, no new failures (same 4 copy-only artifacts as baseline). Done except the Lua dropped-line follow-up.")
inl note_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64_6 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", 6u32, "2026-10-15T23:46Z", "lane-b", "lane-b, cause of the dropped Lua line found (a run-mode capture via a private Kino knob shows the Lua stdout 9007199254740993 / 18446744073709551615 / (empty) / 9007199254740993 / true; the same main.lua through an Erlang port or lua.exe prints all 5 lines). Kino runs Lua cells through the spiral CLI (Builders.argv :lua -> spiral lua --lua-path), whose process_lua (apps/spiral/spiral.spi ~1173-1230) runs the chunk in-process with mlua and replaces only print with custom_print, which collects lines into stdio. io.write (lib console.write on Lua) goes to the host's real stdout, which Kino discards in favour of the JSON output/stdio fields, so any console.write text on Lua is lost in Kino. Fix for tomorrow: in process_lua also set io.write (or a raw buffer shared by print and io.write: print appends args joined by tab plus newline, io.write appends args as-is) and build stdio from that buffer; needs the spiral app rebuild (spiral.livemd -> spi -> rs) and a Kino Lua repro.")
inl note_of_kino_test_cell_i64_as_f64_7 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-CELL-I64-AS-F64", 7u32, "2026-10-15T23:47Z", "main-thread", "19:47 main: closed again; the Lua dropped-line cause is tracked on KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE.")
inl swift_array_reference_semantics () = Task ("SWIFT-ARRAY-REFERENCE-SEMANTICS", "Swift backend copies Spiral arrays (found 19:42 2026-10-15 by the Swift list probe single-flight-20261015-193523): samples/dynamic_array_mutable_alias exits -7 on Swift vs 0 on C, i.e. set inside a join point (write_at) does not reach the caller's array, because Swift [T] is a value type and every join-point argument is a copy; dynamic_array_union_shared_alias and dynamic_array_union_nested_shared_alias fail the same way. Spiral arrays are shared references on every other backend. Fix direction: emit arrays as a final class box (reference) holding the storage, or pass them inout through join points; then re-probe those 3 samples onto the Swift list.", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "swift,correctness,codegen", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_swift_array_reference_semantics () = Planning ("SWIFT-ARRAY-REFERENCE-SEMANTICS", Unestimated, LoadUnset, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_swift_array_reference_semantics_1 () = Note ("SWIFT-ARRAY-REFERENCE-SEMANTICS", 1u32, "2026-10-16T00:06Z", "main-thread", "20:06 main: located in spiral_compiler.fs codegenSwift (shared single-flight section): type YArray -> Array<T> (170622-170625), TyArrayCreate -> Array<T>(repeating:count:) (171074-171080), ArrayIndex a[Int(i)] (171066), ArrayIndexSet a[Int(i)] = v (171069), TyArrayLength Int32(a.count) (171081). Plan: one on-demand helper 'final class SpiralArray<T> { var items: [T]; init(_ items: [T]) { self.items = items } }', YArray -> SpiralArray<T>, create -> SpiralArray(Array(repeating:count:)), index/set/length through .items. Reference semantics then match C/Rust/Zig/Lua; re-probe dynamic_array_mutable_alias, dynamic_array_union_shared_alias, dynamic_array_union_nested_shared_alias onto the Swift list. Expect Swift residual-only changes on every array row in the review.")
inl note_of_swift_array_reference_semantics_2 () = Note ("SWIFT-ARRAY-REFERENCE-SEMANTICS", 2u32, "2026-10-16T00:18Z", "main-thread", "20:18 main: fix proven on a candidate (NOT in the tree): tmp/swiftfix/swift-array-reference.ps1, 6 edits scoped to codegenSwift; candidate built from a job copy (46.6 s), Swift probe single-flight-20261015-201336 (candidate cache): dynamic_array_mutable_alias -7 -> 0, dynamic_array_union_shared_alias and _nested_shared_alias -1 -> 0, all now agree with C; no other Swift verdict or exit changes (507 rows, 366 agree, build-fail 50 as before). Next pack: apply to the tree, review (expect Swift residual-only changes on array rows), add the 3 samples to the Swift list, bless.")
inl note_of_swift_array_reference_semantics_3 () = Note ("SWIFT-ARRAY-REFERENCE-SEMANTICS", 3u32, "2026-10-16T05:16Z", "main-thread", "01:16 main: in pack-1p (tree core): review single-flight-20261016-003349: 69 Swift rows residual-only, behaviour 0; the 3 aliasing samples agree on the candidate and joined the Swift list (343). Install + bless pending.")
inl note_of_swift_array_reference_semantics_4 () = Note ("SWIFT-ARRAY-REFERENCE-SEMANTICS", 4u32, "2026-10-16T06:35Z", "main-thread", "02:35 main: pack-1p installed both modes (single-flight 01:54, gpt5parallel 02:07) and blessed: single-flight-20261016-021005 (6,511 rows, DISAGREE 0) = review 003349 on every cell except portable_convert_parse Gleam residual, which equals the pack-1o bless (the review still had the withdrawn globals change); the 3 Swift aliasing rows and Gleam array_create_reads_zero are listed and agree.")
inl kino_lua_dropped_write () = Task ("KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE", "Kino's Lua run drops a console.write line (found 19:44 2026-10-15 by lane B's i64 probe): Lua shows 4 lines vs Rust 5 for the same test cell; the same program, including Kino's show_value_main wrapper, prints all 5 lines on Lua 5.1 outside Kino. Kino keeps neither the generated main.lua nor a run-mode capture, so the next step is capturing the Lua program and its raw stdout in run mode.", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,lua,correctness", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_lua_dropped_write () = Planning ("KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE", Unestimated, LoadUnset, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kino_lua_dropped_write_1 () = Note ("KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE", 1u32, "2026-10-15T23:47Z", "main-thread", "19:47 main (from lane B): cause found: Kino runs Lua through the spiral CLI (Builders.argv :lua -> spiral lua --lua-path); apps/spiral/spiral.spi process_lua (~1173-1230) runs the chunk in-process with mlua and replaces only print (custom_print -> stdio lines); io.write, used by lib console.write on Lua, goes to the host's real stdout, which Kino ignores. So every console.write text on Lua is lost in Kino, independent of i64. Run-mode capture: line 3 empty; the same main.lua through lua.exe prints all 5. Fix: in process_lua replace io.write too, with one raw buffer (print appends tab-joined args + newline, io.write appends args verbatim), stdio from that buffer; needs the spiral app rebuild + a Kino Lua repro.")
inl note_of_kino_lua_dropped_write_2 () = Note ("KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE", 2u32, "2026-10-16T00:19Z", "main-thread", "20:19 main: fix staged (NOT applied, not built): tmp/luawrite/lua-capture-io-write.ps1, 4 anchors in apps/spiral/spiral.spi process_lua (dry run ok): io.write is replaced too and appends to a pending line; print emits pending ++ its text as one line; a pending line left at the end is flushed. Print-only output stays byte-identical (pending always empty). Proof plan: apply, apps/spiral build (Rust), Kino Lua repro (5 lines vs Rust), Kino Lua sweep 765 cells identical except console.write cells.")
inl note_of_kino_lua_dropped_write_3 () = Note ("KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE", 3u32, "2026-10-16T07:32Z", "main-thread", "03:32 main: the staged tmp/luawrite/lua-capture-io-write.ps1 patches apps/spiral/spiral.spi only, but apps/spiral still has spiral.livemd (13:31) that spiral.spi (13:33) is exported from: apply the same 4 edits to the livemd cells via mix spiral.edit (or migrate apps/spiral off livemd first, BOLD-NATIVE goal), then build.ps1 for the Rust CLI and a Kino Lua console.write repro. Not applied tonight: the compiler packs hold the heavy slot.")
inl note_of_kino_lua_dropped_write_4 () = Note ("KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE", 4u32, "2026-10-16T11:59Z", "main-thread", "07:59 main: the 4 edits are applied to the source of truth: apps/spiral/spiral.livemd cell 90 (process_lua) via mix spiral.edit (4 calls, cell re-rendered with its smart-cell attrs; git diff 5 hunks) and to spiral.spi via tmp/luawrite/lua-capture-io-write.ps1. build.ps1 re-exports spiral.spi from the livemd, so an identical export proves the two agree. Next: apps/spiral build.ps1 (heavy), then the Kino Lua console.write repro.")
inl note_of_kino_lua_dropped_write_5 () = Note ("KINO-LUA-DROPPED-WRITE", 5u32, "2026-10-16T13:13Z", "main-thread", "09:13 main: fixed and built. apps/spiral build.ps1 (exit 0, 131 s, RUST-OK, run checks cuda/lua/gleam ok, new spiral.exe shipped); its livemd export reproduced the scripted spiral.spi byte for byte. Repro tmp/luawrite/repro/src/main.lua (io.write, print, mixed): before, SPIRAL_JSON output was only the print lines and io.write text leaked raw after the JSON; after, output = first line / second<TAB>line / third line / tail without newline and stdout holds only the JSON line. Also a corpus check: pack-1u lib (Kotlin/Swift dispatch) compiles apps/spiral to Rust.")
