inl note_of_x_client_3 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 3u32, "2026-10-16T01:19Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 21:19 -04:00) build.ps1 green: Spiral->Rust compile, cargo release, e2e 8 tutorial steps + 4 extra cases against e2e/stub.py, 4 test blocks in posts/cli/x_api (SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER=process, no daemon left). Live HTTPS check with an invalid token: api.x.com answered 401, decoded as expected (TLS via rustls OK). post.fields=created_at still unverified live.")
inl note_of_x_client_4 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 4u32, "2026-10-16T02:11Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 22:11 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) Renamed from apps/timeline. OAuth2 client credentials (client_credentials grant on /2/oauth2/token with client_type+scope) yield a token the v2 read endpoints refuse (403 Unsupported Authentication 'Unknown'); the app-only Bearer Token from console Keys & Tokens is required. A first Generate was read through the accessibility tree, which truncates at 100 chars (401); the regenerate click was then blocked by the session's permission classifier, so the user copies a fresh token. Client id/secret saved in ~/.secrets/x-api.env (user-only ACL). Live plan: BBCBreaking+SkyNewsBreak (3 follows each), WSJbreakingnews (0 follows).")
inl note_of_x_client_5 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 5u32, "2026-10-16T02:21Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 22:21 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) 280 experiment: 193 top-level blocks all <= 280 X weight (max 276; before: 24 of 96 over, max 1595, measured with a splitter that also glued ///> lines onto the previous block); .spi x-compat findings 0 (whole folder 49 -> 35, all 35 in the tutorial); exe size flat (1,458,688 vs 1,458,176 bytes), generated Rust +6%, source +51% lines (mostly tests). Tests: 22 blocks on zig+rust (prelude 2, posts 3, cli 9, x_api 8 incl. 2 negative GADT tests pinned to their Expected text and mutation-checked). Free live 401 via TLS OK with spindle.exe.")
inl note_of_x_client_6 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 6u32, "2026-10-16T05:40Z", "claude", "2026-10-16 01:40 split into one Rust crate per entry (xc_net, xc_checks, xc_args, xc_users, xc_fetch, xc_refs, xc_write, xc_view, bin xc), crates exchange strings/numbers/tuples; scripts/gate.ps1 reports generated lines vs 1000: all under except xc_view 1786 (code shape, see RUST-UNION-IMPLS and RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION); e2e unchanged; live read OK")
inl note_of_x_client_7 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 7u32, "2026-10-16T11:59Z", "claude", "2026-10-16 07:59 every post, quoted/replied post and repost original ends with [N comments, N reposts, N likes] from public_metrics (reply_count, repost_count, like_count) added to post.fields; same request count (e2e 57 = baseline), no extra billed resource, ~120 bytes more per post; xc_view 1786 -> 1903 generated lines (counts record copied with each post)")
inl note_of_x_client_8 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 8u32, "2026-10-16T15:48Z", "claude", "2026-10-16 11:48 times shown in the time zone of the machine running xc (jiff TimeZone::system, TZ overrides; e2e pins TZ=America/Cuiaba); bare --start-time/--end-time dates are local midnight; names follow the X API: replies (reply_count), username (not handle), --start-time/--end-time (start_time/end_time), [url] hints (entities.urls), 'replied to' (replied_to), X_OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN/X_OAUTH2_REFRESH_TOKEN (were X_USER_*); internal records use API field names (public_metrics, url_entity, media_key, alt_text, next_token, max_results)")
