inl note_of_crate_gate_harden_1 () = Note ("CRATE-GATE-HARDEN", 1u32, "2026-10-16T03:15Z", "main-thread", "23:15 main: evidence 10-15: the gate stopped the strict renewal when agile_todo_scan reached 1,184 (922 .rs + 167 .spi + 95 notebook .spi) and forced a clean split into sources/scan crates; the largest crate after the split is command_spec_domain at 998, so it must be split before the next agile verb.")
inl note_of_crate_gate_harden_2 () = Note ("CRATE-GATE-HARDEN", 2u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night inventory: gated: eoie (crate max 949-998), x (report-only, view.rs 1,885 over); ungated monoliths: apps/spiral spiral.rs 24,281 lines, dice ui main.rs 16,878, dice lib dice.rs 6,639, apps/wasm spiral_wasm.rs 3,464.")
inl x_repo_template () = Task ("X-REPO-TEMPLATE", "i574n/x as the from-scratch Spiral repo template (create-react-app style): find the shape every new Spiral repo should start from; record each decision with its reason and measured cost", Story, P2, D3, 10u32, Planned, "", "template,spiral,x,ci", "current", "current")
inl note_of_x_repo_template_1 () = Note ("X-REPO-TEMPLATE", 1u32, "2026-10-16T03:27Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 23:27 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) Decisions so far: (1) spiral cloned beside the repo (eoie model), no symlinks (dice's deps/polyglot link is the older, slower model) and no SPIRAL_ROOT override, because package.spiproj fixes packageDir ../../../spiral/lib; scripts/common.ps1 resolves XRoot/SpiralRoot and fails with the init hint. (2) scripts/init.ps1 clones spiral from the same owner and runs spiral's init-app-build; scripts/build.ps1 builds every app; scripts/workflow.ps1 = init + build; one CI file .github/workflows/ci.yml (ubuntu + windows) runs workflow.ps1, nothing else standardized (yml standardization stays with the main lane). (3) Root Cargo workspace, stable Rust (generated Rust builds on cargo 1.99.0, no nightly pin), release profile lto+cg1. (4) Kino test blocks run from the sibling Kino with SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER=process (no daemon left), outputs under target/. (5) .gitattributes LF + generated client.rs marked. Measured locally (spiral already beside, 16 GB box, heavy gate): full scripts/build.ps1 517 s (client: cargo cold 130 s, e2e ~60 s, 4 zig test files ~180 s; sim: mix test 30/30, corpus run ~60 s, kino executor run ~30 s); client-only rebuild 345 s. Not measured yet: init from scratch, Linux CI.")
inl note_of_x_repo_template_2 () = Note ("X-REPO-TEMPLATE", 2u32, "2026-10-16T03:31Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 23:31 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) Open decision: the sibling clone tracks spiral's branch tip with no pin. Everything in x was proven against spiral's uncommitted working tree (tonight's compiler packs, other lanes' Kino edits), so CI (init.ps1 clones spiral HEAD) can differ until spiral is committed and pushed. Options: a ref in init.ps1, or a recorded validated spiral commit per x commit. Also measured: stable Rust via rust-toolchain.toml; the generated client builds on cargo 1.99.0.")
inl note_of_x_repo_template_3 () = Note ("X-REPO-TEMPLATE", 3u32, "2026-10-16T05:40Z", "claude", "2026-10-16 01:40 template shape now includes a Cargo workspace of apps/<app>/<crate>/ entries, each Cargo.toml carrying [package.metadata.spiral] entry/output, a metadata-driven build loop, and scripts/gate.ps1 (report-only, -Enforce throws) for the 1000-line generated-file rule")
inl note_of_x_repo_template_4 () = Note ("X-REPO-TEMPLATE", 4u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night inventory of x/scripts (4.5 KB): generic as-is init.ps1 (clone spiral beside from the remote owner and domain, spiral init-app-build), gate.ps1 (1,000-line generated Rust gate over package.metadata.spiral crates) and workflow.ps1; common.ps1 is generic except the XRoot name; only build.ps1 lists the apps. The blog repo is the second consumer to prove the template on.")
inl x_client_token_refresh () = Task ("X-CLIENT-TOKEN-REFRESH", "OAuth 2.0 user access tokens last 2 hours (docs.x.com); with offline.access a refresh token renews them via POST /2/oauth2/token (grant_type=refresh_token, confidential client Basic auth). Add a refresh step that rotates X_USER_TOKEN/X_USER_REFRESH_TOKEN in ~/.secrets/x-api.env without printing them, so the posting key is saved once and never regenerated", Story, P3, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "x,auth", "current", "current")
inl backend_switch_globals_leak () = Task ("BACKEND-SWITCH-GLOBALS-LEAK", "BackendSwitch validation is not hermetic for globals (found 23:58 2026-10-15 while migrating lib is_zig guards): evaluating a non-selected arm for its type runs global calls it reaches, so their text lands in the selected backend's output", TaskKind, P1, D4, 20u32, Planned, "", "compiler,backend-switch,both-cores", "current", "current")
inl note_of_backend_switch_globals_leak_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-GLOBALS-LEAK", 1u32, "2026-10-16T03:58Z", "main-thread", "23:58 main: repro: file_system.file_delete as a backend_switch_or record; on Zig the validated default arm calls trace Critical (Rust path), and trace's own Zig arm registers spiralHold/GetLocalTime/spiralClock globals, which then appear in the Zig output although nothing uses them (probe tmp/dispatchbench probes-before/after file_delete main.zig). AGENTS.md says validation pushes into a throwaway statement list and its own variable counter; globals are not covered. Fix direction (shared section, both cores): snapshot the globals table before validating each non-current arm and restore it afterwards, like the statement list; expect residual-only shrinkage on rows whose records reach global-emitting code. Harmless today (unused definitions), but it makes records emit more than if-guards did.")
inl note_of_backend_switch_globals_leak_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-GLOBALS-LEAK", 2u32, "2026-10-16T05:16Z", "main-thread", "01:16 main: fixed in pack-1p (tree core, both cores): backend_switch_validation_floor names the 1 <<< 30 validation counter base, and the 4 Global sites (single-flight term Global; gpt5parallel term Global, nested term Global, worklist replay, raw unit annotation) record a global only when s.i.contents < floor, i.e. outside any validation, nested evaluations included. Review: 0 harness rows changed by it. Probes on the guard-migrated lib: 17 outputs lose only unreferenced leaked globals (SpiralUse in Rust, std_* type aliases in F#, unused Gleam imports, spiralClock/spiralHold/GetLocalTime in Zig, spiral_node_fs/spiral_trace_state in TypeScript); file_delete Zig is byte-identical to its pre-migration output again. Install + bless pending.")
inl note_of_backend_switch_globals_leak_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-GLOBALS-LEAK", 3u32, "2026-10-16T05:51Z", "main-thread", "01:51 main: fix withdrawn from pack-1p. The corpus check on the candidate failed lib file_system 12/15 (get_source_directory, get_full_path, trace_file: dotnet fsi failed): the suppressed globals included F# type aliases (type std_path_PathBuf = string, std_string_String, Ref) that F# code uses. They come from backend.rust_type -> fsharp_global, called inside Rust arms; in an F# build those arms are only validated, and the nested fsharp_global switch then runs its Fsharp arm with s.backend = Fsharp = env.backend. The compiler comment at the Global site documents this as intended (F#-only declarations run in every build). So the 'leak' is load-bearing for F#. Real fix: make rust_type's F# alias come from the type use (the nominal's F# side) or from a declaration evaluated outside arms, then suppress globals in validation; until then the unused extra globals (Zig spiralClock etc.) stay. Status back to Planned.")
inl note_of_backend_switch_globals_leak_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-GLOBALS-LEAK", 4u32, "2026-10-16T06:35Z", "main-thread", "02:35 main: correction: the withdrawn change did alter one harness row, portable_convert_parse Gleam residual (review 003349 80ff3f0a vs blessed d09c5594, exit and verdict equal). Lib file_system F# is 15/15 on the installed pack-1p without it.")
inl note_of_backend_switch_globals_leak_5 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-GLOBALS-LEAK", 5u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night design conclusion: validation must keep emitting nested Fsharp globals (backend.rust_type F# aliases are needed in F# builds), so the fix is dead-global pruning after codegen, not suppressing globals during validation. Measured: 0 leaked helpers in the 457 sample Zig outputs (only prelude and union constructors are unreferenced) and 0 of 1,551 Rust fns; the leak only shows through lib code (trace), so the check must be a lib Kino probe.")
inl rust_union_impls () = Task ("RUST-UNION-IMPLS", "Rust backend emits an enum plus 'impl tag' and 'impl Default' (about 18 lines) for every union instantiation, and one array-collect loop per element type: x/apps/client/view/view.rs (1786 lines) spends 302 on 17 enum impls and 182 on 8 from_* loops; repro: any crate using list post, list link, list medium, option x -- emit Default/tag only when used, or generically", Story, P3, D4, 85u32, Active, "", "compiler,rust,code-shape", "current", "current")
inl note_of_rust_union_impls_1 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-IMPLS", 1u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: tag half done in staging: pack-c/rust-lazy-tag.ps1 stores each union tag impl and emits it only when a UnionTag op uses it. All 427 Rust rows: 0 behavior cells, 127 residuals; tag impls 194 -> 4 (the 4 are stale outputs, SAMPLES-STALE-OUTPUTS), main.rs -30,353 bytes. Default half: 478 impl Default in 210 files, of which only 57 are reachable from a ::default() use (array creation roots, closure over nested defaults incl. RefCell-wrapped ones; no untyped or derived uses exist), so reachability-based emission drops 421 (88 percent): staged as pack-c/rust-lazy-default.ps1 verified on all Rust rows: 0 behavior cells, 201 residuals, exactly 57 impls left, -52 KB; not yet in a full review. In x/apps/client all 55 Default impls and all tag impls are unused: view.rs 1,885 -> 1,663 lines without them (still over the gate, the rest is RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION), args.rs 995 -> 853. Pack: night pack 10-17 (scripts %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\packs\\night-1017, each with -DryRun; final review single-flight-20261017-053315 on the exact pack: 6,906 rows, DISAGREE 0, residual-only Zig 457 and Rust 415, 3 intended Rust exit cells (shown as 2 NATIVE-DIFF rows); builds in single-flight, hopacsota and gpt5parallel; hopacsota inline and random:23 equal single-flight on every compile and residual cell; corpus 144 of 144; Zig at C speed on the bench).")
inl rust_match_duplication () = Task ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION", "Rust backend duplicates code per match shape: or-patterns copy the arm body per alternative, a '_' arm becomes nested match staircases re-emitting full tuples, two record fields aliasing one runtime value (since/until = '') specialize a function twice, and flattened records are moved through recursion (posts.merge_newest = 107 lines); measured in x/apps/client args (1243 before workarounds) and view", Story, P3, D4, 5u32, Planned, "", "compiler,rust,code-shape", "current", "current")
inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_1 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION", 1u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night measurement (6-line repeated windows, variable numbers normalized): x view.rs 26 percent of 1,884 lines, top window x16 = runs of Rc str clone moves (flattened record fields moved one by one), fetch.rs 18, args.rs 11. The text metric also counts program shape (a mega sample scores 98 from unrolled straight-line code), so the next measure is by AST: clone-move runs and duplicated arm bodies.")
inl spiral_export_pipe_forall () = Task ("SPIRAL-EXPORT-PIPE-FORALL", "Export of an annotated lambda whose body pipes, ((fun t => date_of_text t |> text_or_empty) : string -> string), fails 'Cannot apply a forall with a term' at the pipe; the same body as a named inl (text_or_empty (date_of_text t)) compiles; found in x/apps/client/checks 2026-10-16", TaskKind, P4, D2, 80u32, Active, "", "compiler,spiral,export", "current", "current")
inl note_of_spiral_export_pipe_forall_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EXPORT-PIPE-FORALL", 1u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: root cause Export missing from op_args_inferred (spiral_compiler.fs ~49323), so Infer never fills a forall used inside an exported lambda (Cannot apply a forall with a term). Fix pack-a/export-inferred.ps1; both repros compile on the candidate; no residual change in the full review. Regression case pack-a/export-contract-case.ps1 adds forall_in_export (a 4-line core-free program) to test-rust-exports.ps1: it fails on the installed compiler with Cannot apply a forall with a term and passes on the candidate (all export contracts pass). Lands with PACK-NIGHT-1017. Pack: night pack 10-17 (scripts %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\packs\\night-1017, each with -DryRun; final review single-flight-20261017-053315 on the exact pack: 6,906 rows, DISAGREE 0, residual-only Zig 457 and Rust 415, 3 intended Rust exit cells (shown as 2 NATIVE-DIFF rows); builds in single-flight, hopacsota and gpt5parallel; hopacsota inline and random:23 equal single-flight on every compile and residual cell; corpus 144 of 144; Zig at C speed on the bench).")
inl eoie_topology_crates () = Task ("EOIE-TOPOLOGY-CRATES", "eoie proxy source-topology C:\\home\\git\\x agrees on rust_file_max but reports cargo_crate_max=0: it only recognizes crates in its own layout, not a workspace of apps/<app>/<crate>/Cargo.toml with [package.metadata.spiral] entry/output", TaskKind, P3, D2, 20u32, Active, "", "eoie,eoie-dogfood,x", "current", "current")
inl note_of_eoie_topology_crates_1 () = Note ("EOIE-TOPOLOGY-CRATES", 1u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night, corrected root cause: the generic collector counts crates fine (topology_generic_packages); the verb source_topology_run calls the eoie-layout topology_collect, which only sees <root>/src/<pkg>/Cargo.toml, so x (apps/<app>/<crate>) gets cargo_crate_max=0. Fix: dispatch on layout; it sits in rust_global blob 3 (8,453 chars), so migrate the dispatch to granular Spiral first.")
inl python_int_semantics () = Task ("PYTHON-INT-SEMANTICS", "Python backend integer semantics match C: wrap every fixed-width op, division and remainder toward zero", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,python,backend", "current", "current")
inl note_of_python_int_semantics_1 () = Note ("PYTHON-INT-SEMANTICS", 1u32, "2026-10-16T07:29Z", "main-thread", "03:29 main: diagnosed from codegenPython (spiral_compiler.fs ~175478-175501) and Python probe single-flight-20261015-175614 (39 unlisted DISAGREE): Add/Sub/Mult/Neg/ShiftLeft emit plain Python operators on unbounded ints (no i8..u64 wrap), integer Div is // and Mod is % (both floor; C truncates toward zero, so negatives differ). Failing families: small_int_ops, small_int_scalar, ebpf_arith/bits/conv/div/shift/uacc/umul, lua_wide_integers (wrap/div); managed_string_codepoints/utf8_boundaries/invalid_utf8_slice + string_utf8 (strings are not UTF-8 byte indexed); native_*scc*/recursive_tail_recursion (Python recursion limit); array_create_reads_zero (exit 705). Fix direction: per-width wrap helpers emitted on demand (spiral_wrap_i32 etc., keyed on the operand's YPrim), spiral_div/spiral_mod truncating, sys.setrecursionlimit + a big threading.stack_size main thread. The section maps to upstream's Python generator: keep the ws markers.")
inl note_of_python_int_semantics_2 () = Note ("PYTHON-INT-SEMANTICS", 2u32, "2026-10-16T10:35Z", "main-thread", "06:35 main: scoped in CodegenPython (spiral_compiler.fs ~175495-175546, upstream-mapped section, ws: edits): Add/Sub/Mult/ShiftLeft/Neg/BitwiseComplement emit bare Python ints (no width wrap); Div on ints is // (floors; C truncates toward zero); Mod is % (sign of divisor; C sign of dividend); TyConv is tyv(x) with no wrap or truncation. Plan: one prelude helper per op family emitted on use (Lua's spiral_w64 pattern): spiral_wrap(x, bits, signed) after Add/Sub/Mult/ShiftLeft/Neg/~ and int TyConv, spiral_div_trunc and spiral_mod_trunc for int Div/Mod; arrays already use cp.int32 etc. Prove with -Probe Python -Backend C,Python: the 39 unlisted DISAGREE rows should drop.")
inl note_of_python_int_semantics_3 () = Note ("PYTHON-INT-SEMANTICS", 3u32, "2026-10-16T10:43Z", "main-thread", "06:43 main: prototype proven on a source copy (tmp/pack-t/python-int.ps1; probe single-flight-20261016-063945): 10 of the 39 unlisted DISAGREE now agree (all the integer ones), ts_int_wrap Known -> agree, 0 listed regressions, 159 listed rows residual-only. The remaining 29 are other families (abi_external C ABI x9, dynamic_array x11, UTF-8 strings x4, deep tail recursion x4, array_create_reads_zero): split them out before closing this item. Not in the tree yet.")
inl note_of_python_int_semantics_4 () = Note ("PYTHON-INT-SEMANTICS", 4u32, "2026-10-16T11:57Z", "main-thread", "07:57 main: pack-1s installed both modes (07:23/07:31) and blessed: single-flight-20261016-073131, 6,685 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells against the pack-1r bless 053218 overridden by probes 062511 (Kotlin), 061551 (Swift), 064814 (Python); the one extra row, Bend typecheck_long_let_body, exits 236 like C. ts_int_wrap Python Known -> agree. Python list 383 -> 405. Integer semantics now match C; the rest is PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS / PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM.")
